{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba rs/fq/src/utils.rs'","aggregated_output":"     1\t//! Translation of `quic/utils.h`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! Grab-bag of helpers used throughout the C library: debug\n     4\t//! tracing, sprintf-style formatting, connection-id and address\n     5\t//! manipulation, file open/close wrappers, varint and fixed-width\n     6\t//! frame field codecs, constant-time memcmp, threading primitives,\n     7\t//! a deterministic test RNG, and the test-suite's network simulator\n     8\t//! (sim_link).  No matching `.c` file lives next to the header —\n     9\t//! the bodies are in `quic/util.c` (most of the API), with a\n    10\t//! handful of helpers in `quic/utils.c`-style\n    11\t//! companions.\n    12\t//!\n    13\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies are implemented.  The empty test\n    14\t//! module will be expanded in later phases.\n    15\t//!\n    16\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n    17\t//!\n    18\t//! * `FILE *` → `&mut dyn core::fmt::Write` for *write* sinks\n    19\t//!   (mirrors the convention introduced in\n    20\t//!   [`crate::logger`] and\n    21\t//!   [`crate::config`]).  The persistent\n    22\t//!   debug-output stream installed by [`debug_set_stream`]\n    23\t//!   transfers ownership instead, so the global slot can keep the\n    24\t//!   writer alive between calls.\n    25\t//! * `file_open*` / `file_close` / `file_delete` are real OS file\n    26\t//!   primitives.  They are stubbed here as opaque [`File`] handles;\n    27\t//!   Phase 3 will wire them to `std::fs::File` behind the\n    28\t//!   (not-yet-defined) `std` Cargo feature.\n    29\t//! * `struct sockaddr*` parameters and fields use\n    30\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`] — same convention as\n    31\t//!   [`crate`].  `struct sockaddr_storage*`\n    32\t//!   output parameters fold into `Option<SocketAddr>` (the C\n    33\t//!   `AF_UNSPEC` sentinel becomes `None`).\n    34\t//! * `int`-valued comparators (`compare_addr`,\n    35\t//!   `compare_ip_addr`, `compare_connection_id`,\n    36\t//!   `constant_time_memcmp`) return [`core::cmp::Ordering`]\n    37\t//!   when they are real three-way comparators; the `Boolean-ish`\n    38\t//!   ones (`is_connection_id_null`) become `bool`.\n    39\t//! * `char*` strings: input strings borrow as `&str`; owned outputs\n    40\t//!   return `String`.  Buffer-supplying helpers (e.g.\n    41\t//!   [`addr_text`]) take a `&mut dyn core::fmt::Write`.\n    42\t//! * Threading primitives ([`Thread`], [`Mutex`], [`Event`]) are\n    43\t//!   explicitly out of scope for v1 (\"threading dropped, revisit in\n    44\t//!   v2\" per `TRANSLATE_PLAN.md`).  The types are kept as opaque\n    45\t//!   placeholders so signatures can land; per TRANSLATE_PLAN.md\n    46\t//!   threading support is deferred to v2 and these stubs remain.\n    47\t//! * The C macro `SET_LAST_WAKE(quic, file_id)` and the\n    48\t//!   `DBG_PRINTF` family are bodies-not-signatures: they expand at\n    49\t//!   the call site rather than being declared in the header.  They\n    50\t//!   are deferred to Phase 3 (where the C call sites get\n    51\t//!   translated) — `quic_t` has no `wake_file` /\n    52\t//!   `wake_line` fields yet, so the macro can't be expressed in\n    53\t//!   Rust without redesigning that type.\n    54\t\n    55\tuse core::cmp::Ordering;\n    56\tuse core::net::{IpAddr, SocketAddr};\n    57\tuse std::cell::{Cell, RefCell};\n    58\tuse std::sync::Mutex;\n    59\t\n    60\tuse crate::Error;\n    61\tuse crate::{CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE, ConnectionId, PreferredAddress};\n    62\t\n    63\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    64\t// Tracing / file-id constants.\n    65\t//\n    66\t// Used by the C `SET_LAST_WAKE(quic, file_id)` macro to record\n    67\t// which translation unit last poked the QUIC context.  The macro\n    68\t// itself is deferred — see the module docstring.\n    69\t\n    70\t/// File-id constant for `sender.c`.\n    71\tpub const SENDER: u32 = 1;\n    72\t/// File-id constant for `packet.c`.\n    73\tpub const PACKET: u32 = 2;\n    74\t/// File-id constant for `quicctx.c`.\n    75\tpub const QUICCTX: u32 = 3;\n    76\t/// File-id constant for `frames.c`.\n    77\tpub const FRAME: u32 = 4;\n    78\t/// File-id constant for `loss_recovery.c`.\n    79\tpub const LOSS_RECOVERY: u32 = 5;\n    80\t\n    81\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    82\t// Rate / time / byte conversion (function-like macros in C).\n    83\t\n    84\t/// Bytes that fit on a link of `bps` bytes per second over\n    85\t/// `microseconds`.  C: `BYTES_FROM_RATE`.\n    86\tpub const fn bytes_from_rate(microseconds: u64, bps: u64) -> u64 {\n    87\t    microseconds.wrapping_mul(bps) / 1_000_000\n    88\t}\n    89\t\n    90\t/// Effective rate (bytes per second) implied by sending `bytes`\n    91\t/// in `microseconds`.  C: `RATE_FROM_BYTES`.\n    92\tpub const fn rate_from_bytes(bytes: u64, microseconds: u64) -> u64 {\n    93\t    bytes.wrapping_mul(1_000_000) / microseconds\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    97\t// Filesystem path constants — Linux/macOS layout (the only target\n    98\t// supported in v1; `_WINDOWS` paths are dropped per\n    99\t// `TRANSLATE_PLAN.md`).\n   100\t\n   101\t/// Default solution-relative path used by the test fixtures.\n   102\tpub const DEFAULT_SOLUTION_DIR: &str = \"./\";\n   103\t/// Path separator used to assemble fixture paths.\n   104\tpub const FILE_SEPARATOR: &str = \"/\";\n   105\t\n   106\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   107\t// Debug-printf knobs and tracing helpers.\n   108\t\n   109\t/// Maximum number of trailing characters of `__FILE__` shown by\n   110\t/// the C `DBG_PRINTF` macro (`__FILE__` is right-truncated to the\n   111\t/// last `DBG_PRINTF_FILENAME_MAX` bytes).\n   112\tpub const DBG_PRINTF_FILENAME_MAX: usize = 24;\n   113\t\n   114\t// Thread-local debug state — no Send required; library is single-threaded.\n   115\tthread_local! {\n   116\t    static DEBUG_OUT: RefCell<Option<Box<dyn core::fmt::Write>>> = const { RefCell::new(None) };\n   117\t    static DEBUG_SUSPENDED: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };\n   118\t}\n   119\t\n   120\t// Global solution_dir; typically set once at startup.  Box::leak gives the\n   121\t// returned reference a 'static lifetime at the cost of a one-time allocation.\n   122\tstatic SOLUTION_DIR: Mutex<Option<&'static str>> = Mutex::new(None);\n   123\t\n   124\t/// Install (or clear, with `None`) the global debug-output sink.\n   125\t/// The C signature `void debug_set_stream(FILE *F)` takes a\n   126\t/// borrowed `FILE*`; Rust keeps the sink alive across calls by\n   127\t/// transferring ownership of a `Box<dyn Write>`.  Phase 3 will\n   128\t/// decide whether to expose a borrowed-with-`'static`-lifetime\n   129\t/// alternative.\n   130\tpub fn debug_set_stream(stream: Option<Box<dyn core::fmt::Write>>) {\n   131\t    DEBUG_OUT.with(|o| *o.borrow_mut() = stream);\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\t/// `printf`-style write to the installed debug sink.  The C\n   135\t/// variadic signature `void debug_printf(const char* fmt, ...)`\n   136\t/// becomes a sink for already-formatted text — Rust call sites\n   137\t/// will use `format_args!` / `write!` directly.  The string is\n   138\t/// borrowed for the duration of the call.\n   139\tpub fn debug_printf(msg: &str) {\n   140\t    if DEBUG_SUSPENDED.with(|s| s.get()) {\n   141\t        return;\n   142\t    }\n   143\t    DEBUG_OUT.with(|o| {\n   144\t        if let Some(w) = o.borrow_mut().as_mut() {\n   145\t            let _ = w.write_str(msg);\n   146\t        }\n   147\t    });\n   148\t}\n   149\t\n   150\t/// Push the current debug sink and install a new one.  Mirrors\n   151\t/// `void debug_printf_push_stream(FILE* f)`.  The previously\n   152\t/// installed sink (if any) is saved for [`debug_printf_pop_stream`]\n   153\t/// to restore.\n   154\tpub fn debug_printf_push_stream(stream: Box<dyn core::fmt::Write>) {\n   155\t    DEBUG_OUT.with(|o| {\n   156\t        let mut guard = o.borrow_mut();\n   157\t        assert!(\n   158\t            guard.is_none(),\n   159\t            \"nested debug_printf_push_stream not supported\"\n   160\t        );\n   161\t        *guard = Some(stream);\n   162\t    });\n   163\t}\n   164\t\n   165\t/// Pop the most recently pushed debug sink and restore the saved\n   166\t/// one.  Mirrors `void debug_printf_pop_stream(void)`.\n   167\tpub fn debug_printf_pop_stream() {\n   168\t    DEBUG_OUT.with(|o| {\n   169\t        let mut guard = o.borrow_mut();\n   170\t        assert!(\n   171\t            guard.is_some(),\n   172\t            \"debug_printf_pop_stream: no current stream\"\n   173\t        );\n   174\t        *guard = None;\n   175\t    });\n   176\t}\n   177\t\n   178\t/// Stop logging through the debug sink without tearing it down.\n   179\t/// Mirrors `void debug_printf_suspend(void)`.\n   180\tpub fn debug_printf_suspend() {\n   181\t    DEBUG_SUSPENDED.with(|s| s.set(true));\n   182\t}\n   183\t\n   184\t/// Resume logging through the previously installed debug sink.\n   185\t/// Mirrors `void debug_printf_resume(void)`.\n   186\tpub fn debug_printf_resume() {\n   187\t    DEBUG_SUSPENDED.with(|s| s.set(false));\n   188\t}\n   189\t\n   190\t/// Force the debug suspension flag to `suspended` and return the\n   191\t/// previous value.  C: `int debug_printf_reset(int suspended)`.\n   192\t/// The flag is a 0/1 indicator on both sides, so it maps to\n   193\t/// `bool`.\n   194\tpub fn debug_printf_reset(suspended: bool) -> bool {\n   195\t    DEBUG_SUSPENDED.with(|s| {\n   196\t        let old = s.get();\n   197\t        s.set(suspended);\n   198\t        old\n   199\t    })\n   200\t}\n   201\t\n   202\t/// Hex-dump `bytes` to the debug sink.  C: `void debug_dump(const\n   203\t/// void *x, int len)` — only declared when `_DEBUG` is defined,\n   204\t/// so this entry point is informational in v1.  The C `int len`\n   205\t/// is non-negative in every observed call; mapped to slice length.\n   206\tpub fn debug_dump(bytes: &[u8]) {\n   207\t    if DEBUG_SUSPENDED.with(|s| s.get()) {\n   208\t        return;\n   209\t    }\n   210\t    DEBUG_OUT.with(|o| {\n   211\t        if let Some(w) = o.borrow_mut().as_mut() {\n   212\t            for (i, chunk) in bytes.chunks(16).enumerate() {\n   213\t                let _ = write!(w, \"{:04x}:  \", i * 16);\n   214\t                for b in chunk {\n   215\t                    let _ = write!(w, \"{:02x} \", b);\n   216\t                }\n   217\t                let _ = writeln!(w);\n   218\t            }\n   219\t        }\n   220\t    });\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   224\t// String utilities.\n   225\t\n   226\t// `picoquic_string_create`, `picoquic_string_duplicate`, and\n   227\t// `picoquic_string_free` are subsumed by Rust's owned `String`:\n   228\t// `String::from(s)` replaces the duplicate / create pair, and the\n   229\t// `Drop` impl replaces the `free` shim.  Phase 3 callers should use\n   230\t// owned `String` directly rather than going through helpers.\n   231\t\n   232\t/// Format `args` into the head of `buf` and report bytes written\n   233\t/// via `nb_chars`; truncation returns an `Err`.  C:\n   234\t/// `int sprintf(char* buf, size_t buf_len, size_t* nb_chars,\n   235\t/// const char* fmt, ...)`.\n   236\t///\n   237\t/// The C variadic signature collapses to a single\n   238\t/// pre-formatted `&str` argument, mirroring the convention used\n   239\t/// by [`debug_printf`].  Buffer-overflow returns `Err(())`\n   240\t/// (matching the C `-1`); on success the `Ok(usize)` is the byte\n   241\t/// count written, replacing the `nb_chars` out-parameter.\n   242\tpub fn sprintf(buf: &mut [u8], msg: &str) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n   243\t    let bytes = msg.as_bytes();\n   244\t    if bytes.len() < buf.len() {\n   245\t        buf[..bytes.len()].copy_from_slice(bytes);\n   246\t        buf[bytes.len()] = 0;\n   247\t        Ok(bytes.len())\n   248\t    } else if !buf.is_empty() {\n   249\t        let n = buf.len() - 1;\n   250\t        buf[..n].copy_from_slice(&bytes[..n]);\n   251\t        buf[n] = 0;\n   252\t        Err(Error::BufferTooSmall)\n   253\t    } else {\n   254\t        Err(Error::BufferTooSmall)\n   255\t    }\n   256\t}\n   257\t\n   258\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   259\t// Connection-id helpers.\n   260\t\n   261\t/// All-zero connection id used as a sentinel for \"unset\" / \"none\".\n   262\t/// C: `extern const ConnectionId null_connection_id`.\n   263\tpub const NULL_CONNECTION_ID: ConnectionId = ConnectionId {\n   264\t    id: [0; 20],\n   265\t    id_len: 0,\n   266\t};\n   267\t\n   268\t/// Format the connection id into `bytes` and return the number of\n   269\t/// bytes written.  C: `uint8_t format_connection_id(uint8_t* bytes,\n   270\t/// size_t bytes_max, ConnectionId connection_id)`.\n   271\t///\n   272\t/// Pointer-shape choice: the C body writes through `bytes` for\n   273\t/// `bytes_max` bytes and reports the populated prefix length, so\n   274\t/// `&mut [u8]` carries both pieces of information.  The connection\n   275\t/// id is `Copy`, kept by value as in C.\n   276\tpub fn format_connection_id(bytes: &mut [u8], cnx_id: ConnectionId) -> u8 {\n   277\t    let id_bytes = cnx_id.as_bytes();\n   278\t    let copied = id_bytes.len();\n   279\t    if copied == 0 || copied > bytes.len() {\n   280\t        return 0;\n   281\t    }\n   282\t    bytes[..copied].copy_from_slice(id_bytes);\n   283\t    copied as u8\n   284\t}\n   285\t\n   286\t/// Parse a connection id of `len` bytes from `bytes` into `connection_id`,\n   287\t/// returning the number of bytes consumed.  C:\n   288\t/// `uint8_t parse_connection_id(const uint8_t* bytes, uint8_t len,\n   289\t/// ConnectionId* connection_id)`.\n   290\t///\n   291\t/// The C output parameter becomes the function return:\n   292\t/// `Result<ConnectionId, Error>` reports the parsed id on\n   293\t/// success, `Err(())` on truncation.  The `len` parameter and the\n   294\t/// slice length are redundant in safe Rust; the slice carries it.\n   295\tpub fn parse_connection_id(bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<ConnectionId, Error> {\n   296\t    let len = bytes.len();\n   297\t    if len > CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE {\n   298\t        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n   299\t    }\n   300\t    let mut id = [0u8; CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE];\n   301\t    id[..len].copy_from_slice(bytes);\n   302\t    Ok(ConnectionId {\n   303\t        id,\n   304\t        id_len: len as u8,\n   305\t    })\n   306\t}\n   307\t\n   308\t// `is_null` / cmp / `hash_with_seed` / `val64` live as methods on\n   309\t// [`ConnectionId`] (see `crate::lib`); they were free fns in the\n   310\t// C source.  `Ord` for `ConnectionId` derives the lexicographic\n   311\t// byte-then-length order the C `compare_connection_id` produced.\n   312\t\n   313\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   314\t// Address helpers.\n   315\t\n   316\t/// Pack an IP-and-port into a stable, byte-form key suitable for\n   317\t/// hashing.  C: `size_t hash_addr_bytes(const struct\n   318\t/// sockaddr* addr, uint8_t* bytes)`.  Returns the populated prefix\n   319\t/// length; the C body writes at most 18 bytes (16 for the v6\n   320\t/// address + 2 for the port).\n   321\tpub fn hash_addr_bytes(addr: &SocketAddr, bytes: &mut [u8]) -> usize {\n   322\t    let mut l = 0;\n   323\t    match addr {\n   324\t        SocketAddr::V4(a) => {\n   325\t            let ip = a.ip().octets();\n   326\t            bytes[l..l + 4].copy_from_slice(&ip);\n   327\t            l += 4;\n   328\t            let port = addr.port().to_ne_bytes();\n   329\t            bytes[l..l + 2].copy_from_slice(&port);\n   330\t            l += 2;\n   331\t        }\n   332\t        SocketAddr::V6(a) => {\n   333\t            let ip = a.ip().octets();\n   334\t            bytes[l..l + 16].copy_from_slice(&ip);\n   335\t            l += 16;\n   336\t            let port = addr.port().to_ne_bytes();\n   337\t            bytes[l..l + 2].copy_from_slice(&port);\n   338\t            l += 2;\n   339\t        }\n   340\t    }\n   341\t    l\n   342\t}\n   343\t\n   344\t/// Hash an address with a 16-byte seed.  C: `uint64_t\n   345\t/// hash_addr(const struct sockaddr* addr, const uint8_t*\n   346\t/// hash_seed)`.\n   347\tpub fn hash_addr(addr: &SocketAddr, hash_seed: &[u8; 16]) -> u64 {\n   348\t    let mut bytes = [0u8; 18];\n   349\t    let l = hash_addr_bytes(addr, &mut bytes);\n   350\t    crate::siphash::siphash(&bytes[..l], hash_seed)\n   351\t}\n   352\t\n   353\t/// Decode a hex-coded byte string and write the binary form into\n   354\t/// `bin_output`.  C: `size_t parse_hexa(char const*\n   355\t/// hex_input, size_t input_length, uint8_t* bin_output, size_t\n   356\t/// output_max)`.  Returns the number of bytes decoded.\n   357\t///\n   358\t/// Both length parameters fold into the slice lengths.\n   359\tpub fn parse_hexa(hex_input: &str, bin_output: &mut [u8]) -> usize {\n   360\t    fn hexa_digit(x: u8) -> Option<u8> {\n   361\t        match x {\n   362\t            b'0'..=b'9' => Some(x - b'0'),\n   363\t            b'A'..=b'F' => Some(x - b'A' + 10),\n   364\t            b'a'..=b'f' => Some(x - b'a' + 10),\n   365\t            _ => None,\n   366\t        }\n   367\t    }\n   368\t    let inp = hex_input.as_bytes();\n   369\t    let input_length = inp.len();\n   370\t    if input_length == 0 || (input_length & 1) != 0 || 2 * bin_output.len() < input_length {\n   371\t        return 0;\n   372\t    }\n   373\t    let mut ret = 0;\n   374\t    let mut offset = 0;\n   375\t    while offset < input_length {\n   376\t        match (hexa_digit(inp[offset]), hexa_digit(inp[offset + 1])) {\n   377\t            (Some(av), Some(bv)) => {\n   378\t                bin_output[ret] = (av << 4) | bv;\n   379\t                ret += 1;\n   380\t            }\n   381\t            _ => return 0,\n   382\t        }\n   383\t        offset += 2;\n   384\t    }\n   385\t    ret\n   386\t}\n   387\t\n   388\t/// Parse a hex-coded connection id.  C: `uint8_t\n   389\t/// parse_connection_id_hexa(char const* hex_input, size_t\n   390\t/// input_length, ConnectionId* connection_id)` returning the\n   391\t/// number of bytes decoded; the output parameter folds into the\n   392\t/// `Result` return.\n   393\tpub fn parse_connection_id_hexa(hex_input: &str) -> Result<ConnectionId, Error> {\n   394\t    let mut id = [0u8; CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE];\n   395\t    let len = parse_hexa(hex_input, &mut id[..18]);\n   396\t    Ok(ConnectionId {\n   397\t        id,\n   398\t        id_len: len as u8,\n   399\t    })\n   400\t}\n   401\t\n   402\t/// Print a connection id to a hex string buffer.  C:\n   403\t/// `int print_connection_id_hexa(char* buf, size_t buf_len,\n   404\t/// const ConnectionId* connection_id)` returning 0 / -1.\n   405\t///\n   406\t/// The output buffer becomes a `&mut dyn core::fmt::Write` sink to\n   407\t/// keep the helper `no_std`-friendly (same convention as the\n   408\t/// logger module).  The 0 / -1 status maps to `Result<(), Error>`.\n   409\tpub fn print_connection_id_hexa(\n   410\t    w: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write,\n   411\t    connection_id: &ConnectionId,\n   412\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n   413\t    for b in connection_id.as_bytes() {\n   414\t        write!(w, \"{:02x}\", b).map_err(|_| Error::Generic)?;\n   415\t    }\n   416\t    Ok(())\n   417\t}\n   418\t\n   419\t/// Three-way compare two addresses (IP + port).  C:\n   420\t/// `int compare_addr(const struct sockaddr* expected,\n   421\t/// const struct sockaddr* actual)`.\n   422\tpub fn compare_addr(expected: &SocketAddr, actual: &SocketAddr) -> Ordering {\n   423\t    let ip_cmp = compare_ip_addr(expected, actual);\n   424\t    if ip_cmp == Ordering::Equal {\n   425\t        expected.port().cmp(&actual.port())\n   426\t    } else {\n   427\t        ip_cmp\n   428\t    }\n   429\t}\n   430\t\n   431\t/// Three-way compare just the IP component of two addresses.  C:\n   432\t/// `int compare_ip_addr(const struct sockaddr*, const\n   433\t/// struct sockaddr*)`.\n   434\tpub fn compare_ip_addr(expected: &SocketAddr, actual: &SocketAddr) -> Ordering {\n   435\t    match (expected, actual) {\n   436\t        (SocketAddr::V4(ex), SocketAddr::V4(ac)) => ex.ip().octets().cmp(&ac.ip().octets()),\n   437\t        (SocketAddr::V6(ex), SocketAddr::V6(ac)) => ex.ip().octets().cmp(&ac.ip().octets()),\n   438\t        // AF_INET (2) < AF_INET6 (10 on Linux), so V4 < V6.\n   439\t        (SocketAddr::V4(_), SocketAddr::V6(_)) => Ordering::Less,\n   440\t        (SocketAddr::V6(_), SocketAddr::V4(_)) => Ordering::Greater,\n   441\t    }\n   442\t}\n   443\t\n   444\t/// Read the port number out of an address.  C: `uint16_t\n   445\t/// get_addr_port(const struct sockaddr* addr)`.\n   446\tpub fn get_addr_port(addr: &SocketAddr) -> u16 {\n   447\t    addr.port()\n   448\t}\n   449\t\n   450\t/// Replace the port number on an address.  C declares this with\n   451\t/// `const struct sockaddr*` but the body casts away const and\n   452\t/// writes through the pointer (`util.c:531`).  The Rust signature\n   453\t/// takes a `&mut SocketAddr` to reflect the actual contract.\n   454\tpub fn set_addr_port(addr: &mut SocketAddr, port: u16) {\n   455\t    addr.set_port(port);\n   456\t}\n   457\t\n   458\t/// Length of the platform sockaddr representation in bytes —\n   459\t/// `sizeof(sockaddr_in)` for v4, `sizeof(sockaddr_in6)` for v6,\n   460\t/// `0` for `AF_UNSPEC`.  C: `int addr_length(const struct\n   461\t/// sockaddr* addr)`.  The return value is non-negative; mapped to\n   462\t/// `usize`.\n   463\tpub fn addr_length(addr: &SocketAddr) -> usize {\n   464\t    match addr {\n   465\t        SocketAddr::V4(_) => 16, // sizeof(struct sockaddr_in)\n   466\t        SocketAddr::V6(_) => 28, // sizeof(struct sockaddr_in6)\n   467\t    }\n   468\t}\n   469\t\n   470\t/// Copy an address into a sockaddr_storage slot, treating\n   471\t/// `addr == None` as the C \"zero out the storage\" path.  C:\n   472\t/// `void store_addr(struct sockaddr_storage* stored_addr,\n   473\t/// const struct sockaddr* addr)`.\n   474\t///\n   475\t/// The C output parameter becomes the function return:\n   476\t/// `Option<SocketAddr>` represents stored / cleared respectively.\n   477\tpub fn store_addr(addr: Option<&SocketAddr>) -> Option<SocketAddr> {\n   478\t    addr.copied()\n   479\t}\n   480\t\n   481\t/// Return the IP-bytes (4 or 16) inside a sockaddr.  C:\n   482\t/// `void get_ip_addr(struct sockaddr* addr, uint8_t**\n   483\t/// ip_addr, uint8_t* ip_addr_len)` — both output parameters fold\n   484\t/// into the returned slice.  `None` matches the C path where\n   485\t/// `*ip_addr = NULL; *ip_addr_len = 0;` for unsupported families.\n   486\tpub fn get_ip_addr(_addr: &SocketAddr) -> Option<&[u8]> {\n   487\t    // `SocketAddr` exposes IP octets only by value (`IpAddr::octets()`),\n   488\t    // not by reference; safe Rust cannot produce the required borrow.\n   489\t    // Callers should use `addr.ip()` with `Ipv4Addr::octets()` /\n   490\t    // `Ipv6Addr::octets()` directly.\n   491\t    None\n   492\t}\n   493\t\n   494\t/// Parse `ip_address_text` (IPv4 or IPv6 textual form) and combine\n   495\t/// with `port` into a [`SocketAddr`].  C:\n   496\t/// `int store_text_addr(struct sockaddr_storage* stored_addr,\n   497\t/// const char* ip_address_text, uint16_t port)` returning 0 / -1.\n   498\tpub fn store_text_addr(ip_address_text: &str, port: u16) -> Result<SocketAddr, Error> {\n   499\t    let ip: IpAddr = ip_address_text\n   500\t        .parse()\n   501\t        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n   502\t    Ok(SocketAddr::new(ip, port))\n   503\t}\n   504\t\n   505\t/// Print an address (IP + port) to a `core::fmt::Write` sink.  C:\n   506\t/// `char const* addr_text(const struct sockaddr* addr,\n   507\t/// char* text, size_t text_size)` returns the populated prefix of\n   508\t/// `text`; the Rust translation writes through a sink to stay\n   509\t/// `no_std`-friendly.  The `Err` arm propagates a fmt error.\n   510\tpub fn addr_text(addr: &SocketAddr, w: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write) -> Result<(), core::fmt::Error> {\n   511\t    match addr {\n   512\t        SocketAddr::V4(a) => write!(w, \"{}:{}\", a.ip(), a.port()),\n   513\t        SocketAddr::V6(a) => write!(w, \"[{}]:{}\", a.ip(), a.port()),\n   514\t    }\n   515\t}\n   516\t\n   517\t/// Build the loopback address for the given family + port.  C:\n   518\t/// `int store_loopback_addr(struct sockaddr_storage*\n   519\t/// stored_addr, int addr_family, uint16_t port)` — the family\n   520\t/// argument is one of `AF_INET` / `AF_INET6` and folds into the\n   521\t/// `SocketAddr` variant.\n   522\t///\n   523\t/// `addr_family` stays an `i32` to keep parity with the C ABI;\n   524\t/// callers in the codebase pass the `AF_*` constants directly.\n   525\tpub fn store_loopback_addr(addr_family: i32, port: u16) -> Result<SocketAddr, Error> {\n   526\t    // AF_INET=2 is universal; AF_INET6=10 on Linux, 30 on macOS.\n   527\t    const AF_INET: i32 = 2;\n   528\t    #[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]\n   529\t    const AF_INET6: i32 = 30;\n   530\t    #[cfg(not(target_os = \"macos\"))]\n   531\t    const AF_INET6: i32 = 10;\n   532\t\n   533\t    if addr_family == AF_INET {\n   534\t        store_text_addr(\"127.0.0.1\", port)\n   535\t    } else if addr_family == AF_INET6 {\n   536\t        store_text_addr(\"::1\", port)\n   537\t    } else {\n   538\t        Err(Error::InvalidArgument)\n   539\t    }\n   540\t}\n   541\t\n   542\t/// Fill a preferred-address transport parameter from textual IPv4\n   543\t/// and/or IPv6 addresses.  C: `int set_preferred_address(\n   544\t/// TpPreferredAddress* preferred, char const* v4_text,\n   545\t/// char const* v6_text, uint16_t preferred_port)` returning 0 / -1.\n   546\t///\n   547\t/// Either text argument may be `None` (the C `NULL` selector for\n   548\t/// \"skip this family\").  The function mutates `preferred` in\n   549\t/// place; on `Err(())` the partial state is unspecified, matching\n   550\t/// the C behaviour.\n   551\tpub fn set_preferred_address(\n   552\t    preferred: &mut PreferredAddress,\n   553\t    v4_text: Option<&str>,\n   554\t    v6_text: Option<&str>,\n   555\t    preferred_port: u16,\n   556\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n   557\t    *preferred = PreferredAddress::default();\n   558\t    if let Some(v4) = v4_text {\n   559\t        let addr = store_text_addr(v4, preferred_port)?;\n   560\t        if !matches!(addr, SocketAddr::V4(_)) {\n   561\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n   562\t        }\n   563\t        preferred.v4 = Some(addr);\n   564\t    }\n   565\t    if let Some(v6) = v6_text {\n   566\t        let addr = store_text_addr(v6, preferred_port)?;\n   567\t        if !matches!(addr, SocketAddr::V6(_)) {\n   568\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n   569\t        }\n   570\t        preferred.v6 = Some(addr);\n   571\t    }\n   572\t    Ok(())\n   573\t}\n   574\t\n   575\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   576\t// Solution-dir helpers (test fixtures).\n   577\t\n   578\t/// Set the global solution-relative root used by the test\n   579\t/// fixtures.  C: `void set_solution_dir(char const*\n   580\t/// solution_dir)`.  Passing `None` clears the override.\n   581\tpub fn set_solution_dir(solution_dir: Option<&str>) {\n   582\t    let mut lock = SOLUTION_DIR.lock().unwrap();\n   583\t    *lock = solution_dir.map(|s| -> &'static str { Box::leak(s.to_owned().into_boxed_str()) });\n   584\t}\n   585\t\n   586\t/// Read the global solution-relative root.  C exposes a raw\n   587\t/// `extern char const* solution_dir;` — translated as a\n   588\t/// getter so the global stays behind a safe interface.\n   589\tpub fn solution_dir() -> Option<&'static str> {\n   590\t    *SOLUTION_DIR.lock().unwrap()\n   591\t}\n   592\t\n   593\t/// Compose `solution_path/file_name` (or `./file_name` when\n   594\t/// `solution_path` is `None`) into `target_file_path`.  C:\n   595\t/// `int get_input_path(char* target_file_path, size_t\n   596\t/// file_path_max, const char* solution_path, const char*\n   597\t/// file_name)`.  Buffer overflow returns `Err(())`.\n   598\tpub fn get_input_path(\n   599\t    target_file_path: &mut dyn core::fmt::Write,\n   600\t    solution_path: Option<&str>,\n   601\t    file_name: &str,\n   602\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n   603\t    let solution_path = solution_path.unwrap_or(DEFAULT_SOLUTION_DIR);\n   604\t    let sep = if solution_path.ends_with(FILE_SEPARATOR) {\n   605\t        \"\"\n   606\t    } else {\n   607\t        FILE_SEPARATOR\n   608\t    };\n   609\t    write!(target_file_path, \"{}{}{}\", solution_path, sep, file_name).map_err(|_| Error::Generic)\n   610\t}\n   611\t\n   612\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   613\t// Portable file open / close.\n   614\t//\n   615\t// `picoquic_file_open*` / `picoquic_file_close` only existed to\n   616\t// paper over Windows's `fopen_s` quirk; the Rust translation uses\n   617\t// `std::fs::File` directly at every call site (close = Drop).\n   618\t//\n   619\t// `picoquic_file_delete` survives because callers want a stable\n   620\t// no_std-friendly façade for \"remove this file by name\".  Phase 4\n   621\t// routes the body through `std::fs::remove_file` under the `std`\n   622\t// feature.\n   623\t\n   624\t/// Delete a file by name, returning the OS errno on failure.  C:\n   625\t/// `int picoquic_file_delete(char const* file_name, int* last_err)`.\n   626\tpub fn file_delete(file_name: &(impl AsRef<std::path::Path> + ?Sized)) -> Result<(), i32> {\n   627\t    std::fs::remove_file(file_name).map_err(|e| e.raw_os_error().unwrap_or(-1))\n   628\t}\n   629\t\n   630\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   631\t// Frame skip / decode / encode helpers.\n   632\t//\n   633\t// The C entry points all share a \"cursor pair\" idiom: take\n   634\t// `(bytes, bytes_max)`, advance the cursor and return a pointer\n   635\t// past the parsed field, or `NULL` on overrun.  In Rust the\n   636\t// `&[u8]` slice carries both endpoints; the return value is the\n   637\t// remaining suffix on success or `None` on overrun (the natural\n   638\t// shape of the Rust slice idiom).  Decoded values fold into the\n   639\t// `Ok` payload; encoded outputs fill a pre-allocated buffer and\n   640\t// return the unused tail (or `None` if the buffer was too small).\n   641\t\n   642\t/// Skip `size` bytes from `bytes`; returns the suffix or `None`\n   643\t/// if `bytes` is too short.  C: `frames_fixed_skip`.\n   644\tpub fn frames_fixed_skip(bytes: &[u8], size: u64) -> Option<&[u8]> {\n   645\t    let size = usize::try_from(size).ok()?;\n   646\t    bytes.get(size..)\n   647\t}\n   648\t\n   649\t/// Skip a varint-encoded field; returns the suffix.  C:\n   650\t/// `frames_varint_skip`.\n   651\tpub fn frames_varint_skip(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<&[u8]> {\n   652\t    let v_len = varint_len(*bytes.first()?);\n   653\t    frames_fixed_skip(bytes, v_len as u64)\n   654\t}\n   655\t\n   656\t/// Decode a varint and return the suffix plus the value.  C:\n   657\t/// `frames_varint_decode` with the `*n64` out-parameter\n   658\t/// folded into the tuple return.\n   659\tpub fn frames_varint_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], u64)> {\n   660\t    let first = *bytes.first()?;\n   661\t    let length = varint_len(first);\n   662\t    if bytes.len() < length {\n   663\t        return None;\n   664\t    }\n   665\t    let mut v = (first & 0x3F) as u64;\n   666\t    for &b in &bytes[1..length] {\n   667\t        v <<= 8;\n   668\t        v += b as u64;\n   669\t    }\n   670\t    Some((&bytes[length..], v))\n   671\t}\n   672\t\n   673\t/// Decode a length-prefixed field's length component as a\n   674\t/// `usize`.  C: `frames_varlen_decode`.\n   675\tpub fn frames_varlen_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], usize)> {\n   676\t    let (rest, len) = frames_varint_decode(bytes)?;\n   677\t    let n = usize::try_from(len).ok()?;\n   678\t    Some((rest, n))\n   679\t}\n   680\t\n   681\t/// Decode a single byte.  C: `frames_uint8_decode`.\n   682\tpub fn frames_uint8_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], u8)> {\n   683\t    let (&n, rest) = bytes.split_first()?;\n   684\t    Some((rest, n))\n   685\t}\n   686\t\n   687\t/// Decode a network-order `u16`.  C: `frames_uint16_decode`.\n   688\tpub fn frames_uint16_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], u16)> {\n   689\t    if bytes.len() < 2 {\n   690\t        return None;\n   691\t    }\n   692\t    let n = u16::from_be_bytes([bytes[0], bytes[1]]);\n   693\t    Some((&bytes[2..], n))\n   694\t}\n   695\t\n   696\t/// Decode a network-order `u32`.  C: `frames_uint32_decode`.\n   697\tpub fn frames_uint32_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], u32)> {\n   698\t    if bytes.len() < 4 {\n   699\t        return None;\n   700\t    }\n   701\t    let n = u32::from_be_bytes([bytes[0], bytes[1], bytes[2], bytes[3]]);\n   702\t    Some((&bytes[4..], n))\n   703\t}\n   704\t\n   705\t/// Decode a network-order `u64`.  C: `frames_uint64_decode`.\n   706\tpub fn frames_uint64_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], u64)> {\n   707\t    if bytes.len() < 8 {\n   708\t        return None;\n   709\t    }\n   710\t    let n = u64::from_be_bytes(bytes[..8].try_into().unwrap());\n   711\t    Some((&bytes[8..], n))\n   712\t}\n   713\t\n   714\t/// Skip a length-prefixed data field.  C:\n   715\t/// `frames_length_data_skip`.\n   716\tpub fn frames_length_data_skip(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<&[u8]> {\n   717\t    let (rest, length) = frames_varint_decode(bytes)?;\n   718\t    frames_fixed_skip(rest, length)\n   719\t}\n   720\t\n   721\t/// Decode a connection id and return the suffix.  C:\n   722\t/// `frames_cid_decode`.  The output parameter folds into\n   723\t/// the tuple return.\n   724\tpub fn frames_cid_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(&[u8], ConnectionId)> {\n   725\t    let (rest, id_len) = frames_uint8_decode(bytes)?;\n   726\t    if id_len as usize > CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE || rest.len() < id_len as usize {\n   727\t        return None;\n   728\t    }\n   729\t    let mut id = [0u8; CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE];\n   730\t    id[..id_len as usize].copy_from_slice(&rest[..id_len as usize]);\n   731\t    Some((&rest[id_len as usize..], ConnectionId { id, id_len }))\n   732\t}\n   733\t\n   734\t/// Length of the varint encoding of `n64`.  C:\n   735\t/// `size_t frames_varint_encode_length(uint64_t n64)`.\n   736\tpub fn frames_varint_encode_length(n64: u64) -> usize {\n   737\t    if n64 < 64 {\n   738\t        1\n   739\t    } else if n64 < 16384 {\n   740\t        2\n   741\t    } else if n64 < 1073741824 {\n   742\t        4\n   743\t    } else {\n   744\t        8\n   745\t    }\n   746\t}\n   747\t\n   748\t/// Decode the wire length of a varint from its first byte.  C\n   749\t/// macro: `VARINT_LEN(bytes) (((uint8_t)1) << ((bytes[0] >> 6) & 3))`.\n   750\t/// The macro takes the whole buffer; the function takes just the\n   751\t/// first byte (the rest is unused in the C expansion).\n   752\tpub const fn varint_len(byte0: u8) -> usize {\n   753\t    1usize << ((byte0 >> 6) & 3)\n   754\t}\n   755\t\n   756\t/// Encode a varint into `bytes`; returns the unused tail or `None`\n   757\t/// if the buffer was too small.  C: `frames_varint_encode`.\n   758\tpub fn frames_varint_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n64: u64) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   759\t    if n64 < 64 {\n   760\t        if bytes.is_empty() {\n   761\t            return None;\n   762\t        }\n   763\t        bytes[0] = n64 as u8;\n   764\t        Some(&mut bytes[1..])\n   765\t    } else if n64 < 16384 {\n   766\t        if bytes.len() < 2 {\n   767\t            return None;\n   768\t        }\n   769\t        bytes[0] = ((n64 >> 8) | 0x40) as u8;\n   770\t        bytes[1] = n64 as u8;\n   771\t        Some(&mut bytes[2..])\n   772\t    } else if n64 < 1073741824 {\n   773\t        if bytes.len() < 4 {\n   774\t            return None;\n   775\t        }\n   776\t        bytes[0] = ((n64 >> 24) | 0x80) as u8;\n   777\t        bytes[1] = (n64 >> 16) as u8;\n   778\t        bytes[2] = (n64 >> 8) as u8;\n   779\t        bytes[3] = n64 as u8;\n   780\t        Some(&mut bytes[4..])\n   781\t    } else {\n   782\t        if bytes.len() < 8 {\n   783\t            return None;\n   784\t        }\n   785\t        bytes[0] = ((n64 >> 56) | 0xC0) as u8;\n   786\t        bytes[1] = (n64 >> 48) as u8;\n   787\t        bytes[2] = (n64 >> 40) as u8;\n   788\t        bytes[3] = (n64 >> 32) as u8;\n   789\t        bytes[4] = (n64 >> 24) as u8;\n   790\t        bytes[5] = (n64 >> 16) as u8;\n   791\t        bytes[6] = (n64 >> 8) as u8;\n   792\t        bytes[7] = n64 as u8;\n   793\t        Some(&mut bytes[8..])\n   794\t    }\n   795\t}\n   796\t\n   797\t/// Encode a `usize` as a varint length prefix.  C:\n   798\t/// `frames_varlen_encode`.\n   799\tpub fn frames_varlen_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: usize) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   800\t    frames_varint_encode(bytes, n as u64)\n   801\t}\n   802\t\n   803\t/// Encode a single byte.  C: `frames_uint8_encode`.\n   804\tpub fn frames_uint8_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: u8) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   805\t    if bytes.is_empty() {\n   806\t        return None;\n   807\t    }\n   808\t    bytes[0] = n;\n   809\t    Some(&mut bytes[1..])\n   810\t}\n   811\t\n   812\t/// Encode a network-order `u16`.  C: `frames_uint16_encode`.\n   813\tpub fn frames_uint16_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: u16) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   814\t    if bytes.len() < 2 {\n   815\t        return None;\n   816\t    }\n   817\t    bytes[0] = (n >> 8) as u8;\n   818\t    bytes[1] = n as u8;\n   819\t    Some(&mut bytes[2..])\n   820\t}\n   821\t\n   822\t/// Encode a 24-bit value (low three bytes of `n`) in network\n   823\t/// order.  C: `frames_uint24_encode`.\n   824\tpub fn frames_uint24_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: u32) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   825\t    if bytes.len() < 3 {\n   826\t        return None;\n   827\t    }\n   828\t    bytes[0] = (n >> 16) as u8;\n   829\t    bytes[1] = (n >> 8) as u8;\n   830\t    bytes[2] = n as u8;\n   831\t    Some(&mut bytes[3..])\n   832\t}\n   833\t\n   834\t/// Encode a network-order `u32`.  C: `frames_uint32_encode`.\n   835\tpub fn frames_uint32_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: u32) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   836\t    if bytes.len() < 4 {\n   837\t        return None;\n   838\t    }\n   839\t    bytes[0] = (n >> 24) as u8;\n   840\t    bytes[1] = (n >> 16) as u8;\n   841\t    bytes[2] = (n >> 8) as u8;\n   842\t    bytes[3] = n as u8;\n   843\t    Some(&mut bytes[4..])\n   844\t}\n   845\t\n   846\t/// Encode a network-order `u64`.  C: `frames_uint64_encode`.\n   847\tpub fn frames_uint64_encode(bytes: &mut [u8], n: u64) -> Option<&mut [u8]> {\n   848\t    if bytes.len() < 8 {\n   849\t        return None;\n   850\t    }\n   851\t    bytes[0] = (n >> 56) as u8;\n   852\t    bytes[1] = (n >> 48) as u8;\n   853\t    bytes[2] = (n >> 40) as u8;\n   854\t    bytes[3] = (n >> 32) as u8;\n   855\t    bytes[4] = (n >> 24) as u8;\n   856\t    bytes[5] = (n >> 16) as u8;\n   857\t    bytes[6] = (n >> 8) as u8;\n   858\t    bytes[7] = n as u8;\n   859\t    Some(&mut bytes[8..])\n   860\t}\n   861\t\n   862\t/// Encode a length prefix followed by the data bytes.  C:\n   863\t/// `frames_length_data_encode`.  The C signature took\n   864\t/// `(size_t l, const uint8_t* v)` — collapsed to `&[u8]` (slice\n   865\t/// length subsumes `l`).\n   866\tpub fn frames_length_data_encode<'a>(bytes: &'a mut [u8], v: &[u8]) -> Option<&'a mut [u8]> {\n   867\t    let l = v.len();\n   868\t    let rest = frames_varlen_encode(bytes, l)?;\n   869\t    if rest.len() < l {\n   870\t        return None;\n   871\t    }\n   872\t    rest[..l].copy_from_slice(v);\n   873\t    Some(&mut rest[l..])\n   874\t}\n   875\t\n   876\t/// Encode a connection id as length-prefixed data.  C:\n   877\t/// `frames_cid_encode`.\n   878\tpub fn frames_cid_encode<'a>(bytes: &'a mut [u8], cid: &ConnectionId) -> Option<&'a mut [u8]> {\n   879\t    frames_length_data_encode(bytes, cid.as_bytes())\n   880\t}\n   881\t\n   882\t/// Encode a NUL-terminated C string `s` as length-prefixed data\n   883\t/// (the NUL is *not* written).  C: `frames_charz_encode`.\n   884\tpub fn frames_charz_encode<'a>(bytes: &'a mut [u8], s: &str) -> Option<&'a mut [u8]> {\n   885\t    frames_length_data_encode(bytes, s.as_bytes())\n   886\t}\n   887\t\n   888\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   889\t// Constant-time memcmp (used for reset secrets).\n   890\t\n   891\t/// Constant-time three-way compare of two byte buffers of equal\n   892\t/// length.  C: `int constant_time_memcmp(const uint8_t*\n   893\t/// x, const uint8_t* y, size_t l)` — returning negative / zero /\n   894\t/// positive, mapped to [`Ordering`].  The two slice lengths are\n   895\t/// the C `l` argument and must match.\n   896\tpub fn constant_time_memcmp(x: &[u8], y: &[u8]) -> Ordering {\n   897\t    let mut acc: u64 = 0;\n   898\t    for (&xi, &yi) in x.iter().zip(y.iter()) {\n   899\t        acc += (xi ^ yi) as u64;\n   900\t    }\n   901\t    if acc == 0 {\n   902\t        Ordering::Equal\n   903\t    } else {\n   904\t        Ordering::Less\n   905\t    }\n   906\t}\n   907\t\n   908\t// The C `picoquic_thread_t` / `picoquic_mutex_t` / `picoquic_event_t`\n   909\t// portability wrappers around pthread / Win32 are gone.  Rust call\n   910\t// sites use the standard library directly: `std::thread::JoinHandle`\n   911\t// for a thread handle, `std::sync::Mutex<T>` for a lock paired with\n   912\t// the value it guards, and `(Mutex<bool>, Condvar)` (or a higher-level\n   913\t// channel from `std::sync::mpsc`) where C used `picoquic_event_t`.\n   914\t//\n   915\t// Likewise the `picoquic_thread_fn` typedef has no Rust counterpart —\n   916\t// `std::thread::spawn` already takes an arbitrary `FnOnce() + Send`\n   917\t// closure, which subsumes the C \"function pointer + void* arg\"\n   918\t// pattern.\n   919\t\n   920\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   921\t// Random-number helpers.\n   922\t\n   923\t// `uniform_random` is gone -- the C body read `/dev/urandom`\n   924\t// at every call.  Rust callers use `rand::Rng::random_range`\n   925\t// on whatever RNG they hold (`Quic.rng` for the secure stream,\n   926\t// `rand::rng()` for the non-secure thread-local).\n   927\t\n   928\t// `test_random` and the `test_*_random` family moved to\n   929\t// `crate::tests::util` — they only support the test suite.\n   930\t\n   931\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   932\t// Byte-array → text conversion (logging helper).\n   933\t\n   934\t/// Translate a byte buffer to a printable text form.  C:\n   935\t/// `char* uint8_to_str(char* text, size_t text_len, const\n   936\t/// uint8_t* data, size_t data_len)` — both length parameters fold\n   937\t/// into the slice lengths.  The returned slice is the populated\n   938\t/// prefix of `text`.\n   939\tpub fn uint8_to_str<'a>(text: &'a mut [u8], data: &[u8]) -> &'a [u8] {\n   940\t    let text_len = text.len();\n   941\t    let data_len = data.len();\n   942\t    let render_length = if data_len >= text_len {\n   943\t        text_len.saturating_sub(4)\n   944\t    } else {\n   945\t        data_len\n   946\t    };\n   947\t    let mut rendered = 0usize;\n   948\t    for &c in &data[..render_length] {\n   949\t        text[rendered] = if (b' '..127).contains(&c) { c } else { b'?' };\n   950\t        rendered += 1;\n   951\t    }\n   952\t    if rendered < data_len {\n   953\t        let mut i = 0usize;\n   954\t        while i < 3 && rendered + 1 < text_len {\n   955\t            text[rendered] = b'.';\n   956\t            rendered += 1;\n   957\t            i += 1;\n   958\t        }\n   959\t    }\n   960\t    if rendered < text_len {\n   961\t        text[rendered] = 0;\n   962\t    }\n   963\t    &text[..rendered]\n   964\t}\n   965\t\n   966\t// `TestSimPacket`, `TestAqm`, `JitterMode`, and `TestSimLink`\n   967\t// moved to `crate::tests::util` — they translate the\n   968\t// `picoquictest/sim_link.c` test-only network simulator.\n   969\t// `TEST_SNI` and the `TEST_FILE_*` / `TEST_ECH_*` cert-path\n   970\t// constants likewise moved over.\n   971\t\n   972\t#[cfg(test)]\n   973\tmod test {}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba rs/fq/src/tests/cnxstress.rs'","aggregated_output":"     1\t//! Test cases for `picoquictest/cnxstress.c`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! Exercises connection-level stress — multiple parallel client connections,\n     4\t//! message passing, connection teardown — and connection-limit enforcement.\n     5\t//!\n     6\t//! The stress context creates a server `Quic`, a client `Quic`, and two\n     7\t//! simulated links.  A loop drives connection setup, message exchange, and\n     8\t//! teardown.  `cnx_limit` verifies that the stack sends `SERVER_BUSY` when\n     9\t//! the connection table is full.\n    10\t\n    11\tuse std::cell::RefCell;\n    12\tuse std::rc::Rc;\n    13\t\n    14\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n    15\t\n    16\tuse crate::errors::TransportError;\n    17\tuse crate::tests::util::{\n    18\t    TEST_FILE_SERVER_CERT, TEST_FILE_SERVER_KEY, TestSimLink, TestSimPacket, test_random,\n    19\t};\n    20\tuse crate::tp::TransportParameters;\n    21\tuse crate::{\n    22\t    CallbackEvent, Connection, ConnectionId, Duration, Error, Instant, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE,\n    23\t    State, StreamDataCallback, current_time,\n    24\t};\n    25\t\n    26\tconst CNX_STRESS_ALPN: &str = \"cnxstress\";\n    27\t\n    28\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    29\t// Stream context.\n    30\t\n    31\t/// Per-stream state for both sending and receiving sides.\n    32\t/// C: `cnx_stress_stream_ctx_t`.\n    33\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n    34\tstruct CnxStressStreamCtx {\n    35\t    stream_id: u64,\n    36\t    /// Timestamp embedded in the first 8 bytes of the message payload.\n    37\t    send_time: u64,\n    38\t    /// Total message size encoded in bytes 8–15.\n    39\t    nb_bytes_expected: u64,\n    40\t    nb_bytes_received: u64,\n    41\t    nb_bytes_sent: u64,\n    42\t}\n    43\t\n    44\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    45\t// Shared state (callback ↔ outer loop).\n    46\t\n    47\t/// Fields that both the connection callbacks and the outer simulation loop\n    48\t/// read or write.  Wrapped in `Rc<RefCell<>>` so callbacks can hold a clone.\n    49\t/// C: the callback-mutated subset of `cnx_stress_ctx_t`.\n    50\tstruct CnxStressShared {\n    51\t    nb_clients: usize,\n    52\t    nb_servers: usize,\n    53\t    nb_clients_deleted: usize,\n    54\t    /// `c_active[rank]` is `true` while the client connection at that slot\n    55\t    /// is live.  Set to `false` in the close/application_close callback.\n    56\t    c_active: Vec<bool>,\n    57\t    /// Same for server-side connections.\n    58\t    s_active: Vec<bool>,\n    59\t    is_limit_test: bool,\n    60\t    limit_test_got_server_busy: bool,\n    61\t    nb_client_target: usize,\n    62\t    nb_messages_target: usize,\n    63\t    message_size: u64,\n    64\t    nb_messages_sent: usize,\n    65\t    nb_messages_errors: usize,\n    66\t    nb_messages_received: usize,\n    67\t    sum_message_delays: i64,\n    68\t    sum_square_message_delays: f64,\n    69\t    message_delay_min: i64,\n    70\t    message_delay_max: i64,\n    71\t    /// Mirrors `CnxStressCtx::simulated_time`; updated each loop iteration so\n    72\t    /// callbacks can compute `time_now – send_time` without access to the\n    73\t    /// outer context.  C: obtained via `picoquic_get_quic_time(cnx->quic)`.\n    74\t    simulated_time: u64,\n    75\t}\n    76\t\n    77\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    78\t// Outer simulation loop context.\n    79\t\n    80\t/// Full simulation state.  C: `cnx_stress_ctx_t`.\n    81\tstruct CnxStressCtx {\n    82\t    shared: Rc<RefCell<CnxStressShared>>,\n    83\t    qserver: Box<Quic>,\n    84\t    qclient: Box<Quic>,\n    85\t    server_addr: SocketAddr,\n    86\t    client_addr: SocketAddr,\n    87\t    link_to_clients: Box<TestSimLink>,\n    88\t    link_to_server: Box<TestSimLink>,\n    89\t    client_creation_interval: u64,\n    90\t    next_client_creation_time: u64,\n    91\t    client_deletion_interval: u64,\n    92\t    next_client_deletion_time: u64,\n    93\t    message_creation_interval: u64,\n    94\t    next_message_creation_time: u64,\n    95\t    /// Initial source CIDs of client connections, indexed by rank.\n    96\t    /// `None` means the slot is vacant (never filled or connection closed).\n    97\t    client_connections: Vec<Option<ConnectionId>>,\n    98\t    /// Same for server-side connections.\n    99\t    server_connections: Vec<Option<ConnectionId>>,\n   100\t}\n   101\t\n   102\timpl CnxStressCtx {\n   103\t    fn simulated_time(&self) -> u64 {\n   104\t        self.shared.borrow().simulated_time\n   105\t    }\n   106\t}\n   107\t\n   108\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   109\t// Connection callback.\n   110\t\n   111\t/// Per-connection callback context.  C: `cnx_stress_callback_ctx_t`.\n   112\t///\n   113\t/// `mode` values:\n   114\t/// * `0` — client connection\n   115\t/// * `1` — server connection (created after the default context fires)\n   116\t/// * `2` — default server context (installed on `qserver`); on the first\n   117\t///   non-close event it replaces itself with a mode-1 callback.\n   118\tstruct CnxStressCallback {\n   119\t    shared: Rc<RefCell<CnxStressShared>>,\n   120\t    mode: i32,\n   121\t    rank: usize,\n   122\t    streams: Vec<CnxStressStreamCtx>,\n   123\t}\n   124\t\n   125\timpl CnxStressCallback {\n   126\t    fn find_stream_mut(&mut self, stream_id: u64) -> Option<&mut CnxStressStreamCtx> {\n   127\t        self.streams.iter_mut().find(|s| s.stream_id == stream_id)\n   128\t    }\n   129\t\n   130\t    fn create_stream(&mut self, stream_id: u64) -> &mut CnxStressStreamCtx {\n   131\t        self.streams.push(CnxStressStreamCtx {\n   132\t            stream_id,\n   133\t            send_time: 0,\n   134\t            nb_bytes_expected: 0,\n   135\t            nb_bytes_received: 0,\n   136\t            nb_bytes_sent: 0,\n   137\t        });\n   138\t        self.streams.last_mut().unwrap()\n   139\t    }\n   140\t\n   141\t    fn delete_stream(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, stream_id: u64) {\n   142\t        connection.unlink_app_stream_ctx(stream_id);\n   143\t        self.streams.retain(|s| s.stream_id != stream_id);\n   144\t    }\n   145\t\n   146\t    /// Handle incoming stream data / FIN.\n   147\t    /// C: `cnx_stress_callback_data`.\n   148\t    fn handle_data(\n   149\t        &mut self,\n   150\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n   151\t        stream_id: u64,\n   152\t        bytes: &[u8],\n   153\t        is_fin: bool,\n   154\t    ) -> i32 {\n   155\t        if self.find_stream_mut(stream_id).is_none() {\n   156\t            let stream = self.create_stream(stream_id);\n   157\t            stream.stream_id = stream_id;\n   158\t            if connection.set_app_stream_ctx(stream_id, None).is_err() {\n   159\t                return -1;\n   160\t            }\n   161\t        }\n   162\t        let stream = self.find_stream_mut(stream_id).unwrap();\n   163\t        let mut pos = 0usize;\n   164\t        let buf = bytes;\n   165\t        while pos < buf.len() && stream.nb_bytes_received < 8 {\n   166\t            stream.send_time = (stream.send_time << 8) | buf[pos] as u64;\n   167\t            pos += 1;\n   168\t            stream.nb_bytes_received += 1;\n   169\t        }\n   170\t        while pos < buf.len() && stream.nb_bytes_received < 16 {\n   171\t            stream.nb_bytes_expected = (stream.nb_bytes_expected << 8) | buf[pos] as u64;\n   172\t            pos += 1;\n   173\t            stream.nb_bytes_received += 1;\n   174\t        }\n   175\t        stream.nb_bytes_received += (buf.len() - pos) as u64;\n   176\t\n   177\t        if is_fin {\n   178\t            let (recv, expected, send_time) = (\n   179\t                stream.nb_bytes_received,\n   180\t                stream.nb_bytes_expected,\n   181\t                stream.send_time,\n   182\t            );\n   183\t            {\n   184\t                let mut shared = self.shared.borrow_mut();\n   185\t                if recv < 16 || recv < expected {\n   186\t                    shared.nb_messages_errors += 1;\n   187\t                } else {\n   188\t                    let time_now = shared.simulated_time;\n   189\t                    let delta_t = time_now as i64 - send_time as i64;\n   190\t                    shared.nb_messages_received += 1;\n   191\t                    shared.sum_message_delays += delta_t;\n   192\t                    shared.sum_square_message_delays += (delta_t as f64) * (delta_t as f64);\n   193\t                    if delta_t > shared.message_delay_max {\n   194\t                        shared.message_delay_max = delta_t;\n   195\t                    }\n   196\t                    if delta_t < shared.message_delay_min {\n   197\t                        shared.message_delay_min = delta_t;\n   198\t                    }\n   199\t                }\n   200\t            }\n   201\t            self.delete_stream(connection, stream_id);\n   202\t        }\n   203\t        0\n   204\t    }\n   205\t\n   206\t    /// Called when the connection is closed (any flavour).\n   207\t    /// C: `cnx_stress_callback_delete_context`.\n   208\t    fn handle_close(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection) {\n   209\t        {\n   210\t            let mut shared = self.shared.borrow_mut();\n   211\t            if self.mode == 0 {\n   212\t                if shared.is_limit_test\n   213\t                    && self.rank + 1 == shared.nb_client_target\n   214\t                    && connection.state() == State::Disconnected\n   215\t                    && connection.remote_error() == TransportError::ServerBusy as u64\n   216\t                {\n   217\t                    shared.limit_test_got_server_busy = true;\n   218\t                }\n   219\t                if self.rank < shared.c_active.len() {\n   220\t                    shared.c_active[self.rank] = false;\n   221\t                }\n   222\t            } else if self.mode == 1 && self.rank < shared.s_active.len() {\n   223\t                shared.s_active[self.rank] = false;\n   224\t            }\n   225\t        }\n   226\t        // Drain remaining stream contexts.\n   227\t        let stream_ids: Vec<u64> = self.streams.iter().map(|s| s.stream_id).collect();\n   228\t        for sid in stream_ids {\n   229\t            connection.unlink_app_stream_ctx(sid);\n   230\t        }\n   231\t        self.streams.clear();\n   232\t        connection.set_callback(None);\n   233\t    }\n   234\t}\n   235\t\n   236\timpl StreamDataCallback for CnxStressCallback {\n   237\t    fn callback(\n   238\t        &mut self,\n   239\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n   240\t        stream_id: u64,\n   241\t        bytes: &[u8],\n   242\t        fin_or_event: CallbackEvent,\n   243\t        _stream_ctx: Option<&mut dyn core::any::Any>,\n   244\t    ) -> i32 {\n   245\t        // Default context (mode == 2): on first real event, spawn a mode-1\n   246\t        // server context and install it on the connection.\n   247\t        if self.mode == 2 {\n   248\t            match fin_or_event {\n   249\t                CallbackEvent::StatelessReset\n   250\t                | CallbackEvent::Close\n   251\t                | CallbackEvent::ApplicationClose => return 0,\n   252\t                _ => {\n   253\t                    let new_rank = {\n   254\t                        let mut shared = self.shared.borrow_mut();\n   255\t                        let rank = shared.nb_servers;\n   256\t                        if rank < shared.s_active.len() {\n   257\t                            shared.s_active[rank] = true;\n   258\t                        }\n   259\t                        shared.nb_servers += 1;\n   260\t                        rank\n   261\t                    };\n   262\t                    let new_cb = Box::new(CnxStressCallback {\n   263\t                        shared: Rc::clone(&self.shared),\n   264\t                        mode: 1,\n   265\t                        rank: new_rank,\n   266\t                        streams: Vec::new(),\n   267\t                    });\n   268\t                    connection.set_callback(Some(new_cb));\n   269\t                    // The new callback will handle subsequent events; for the\n   270\t                    // current delivery the stack will re-invoke after set_callback.\n   271\t                    return 0;\n   272\t                }\n   273\t            }\n   274\t        }\n   275\t\n   276\t        match fin_or_event {\n   277\t            CallbackEvent::StreamData => self.handle_data(connection, stream_id, bytes, false),\n   278\t            CallbackEvent::StreamFin => self.handle_data(connection, stream_id, bytes, true),\n   279\t            CallbackEvent::StreamReset => {\n   280\t                self.shared.borrow_mut().nb_messages_errors += 1;\n   281\t                self.delete_stream(connection, stream_id);\n   282\t                0\n   283\t            }\n   284\t            CallbackEvent::StopSending => 0,\n   285\t            CallbackEvent::StatelessReset\n   286\t            | CallbackEvent::Close\n   287\t            | CallbackEvent::ApplicationClose => {\n   288\t                self.handle_close(connection);\n   289\t                0\n   290\t            }\n   291\t            CallbackEvent::StreamGap => 0,\n   292\t            CallbackEvent::PrepareToSend => {\n   293\t                // The prepare-to-send path calls `provide_stream_data_buffer`\n   294\t                // with the buffer-argument context.  The current Rust\n   295\t                // `StreamDataCallback` signature passes that argument through\n   296\t                // `bytes: &[u8]`, which is immutable; the API surface for\n   297\t                // mutable buffer provision is not yet fully resolved.\n   298\t                todo!(\n   299\t                    \"PrepareToSend: provide_stream_data_buffer context not yet resolved in Rust API\"\n   300\t                )\n   301\t            }\n   302\t            CallbackEvent::AlmostReady | CallbackEvent::Ready => 0,\n   303\t            CallbackEvent::Datagram => 0,\n   304\t            CallbackEvent::VersionNegotiation => 0,\n   305\t            CallbackEvent::RequestAlpnList | CallbackEvent::SetAlpn => 0,\n   306\t            _ => 0,\n   307\t        }\n   308\t    }\n   309\t}\n   310\t\n   311\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   312\t// Simulation helpers.\n   313\t\n   314\t/// Find an active connection slot, cycling from `msg_num % nb_ctx`.\n   315\t/// C: `cnx_stress_cnx_from_rank`.\n   316\tfn cnx_stress_cnx_from_rank(\n   317\t    msg_num: usize,\n   318\t    nb_ctx: usize,\n   319\t    active: &[bool],\n   320\t    connections: &[Option<ConnectionId>],\n   321\t) -> Option<(usize, ConnectionId)> {\n   322\t    if nb_ctx == 0 {\n   323\t        return None;\n   324\t    }\n   325\t    let start = msg_num % nb_ctx;\n   326\t    for i in 0..nb_ctx {\n   327\t        let rank = (start + i) % nb_ctx;\n   328\t        if active.get(rank).copied().unwrap_or(false)\n   329\t            && let Some(Some(cid)) = connections.get(rank)\n   330\t        {\n   331\t            return Some((rank, *cid));\n   332\t        }\n   333\t    }\n   334\t    None\n   335\t}\n   336\t\n   337\t/// Initiate a new unidirectional message stream on an active connection.\n   338\t/// C: `cnx_stress_initiate_message`.\n   339\tfn cnx_stress_initiate_message(ctx: &mut CnxStressCtx) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   340\t    let (is_client_turn, nb_ctx, message_size, msg_num) = {\n   341\t        let mut shared = ctx.shared.borrow_mut();\n   342\t        shared.nb_messages_sent += 1;\n   343\t        let is_client = (shared.nb_messages_sent & 1) != 0;\n   344\t        let nb = if is_client {\n   345\t            shared.nb_clients\n   346\t        } else {\n   347\t            shared.nb_servers\n   348\t        };\n   349\t        (is_client, nb, shared.message_size, shared.nb_messages_sent)\n   350\t    };\n   351\t\n   352\t    let slot = {\n   353\t        let shared = ctx.shared.borrow();\n   354\t        let active = if is_client_turn {\n   355\t            &shared.c_active\n   356\t        } else {\n   357\t            &shared.s_active\n   358\t        };\n   359\t        let conns = if is_client_turn {\n   360\t            &ctx.client_connections\n   361\t        } else {\n   362\t            &ctx.server_connections\n   363\t        };\n   364\t        cnx_stress_cnx_from_rank(msg_num, nb_ctx, active, conns)\n   365\t    };\n   366\t\n   367\t    let (_rank, cid) = slot.ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n   368\t    let simulated_time = ctx.simulated_time();\n   369\t    let quic = if is_client_turn {\n   370\t        &mut ctx.qclient\n   371\t    } else {\n   372\t        &mut ctx.qserver\n   373\t    };\n   374\t    let connection = quic.connection_ref_by_id(cid).ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n   375\t    let stream_id = connection.get_next_local_stream_id(true);\n   376\t    let stream_ctx = CnxStressStreamCtx {\n   377\t        stream_id,\n   378\t        send_time: simulated_time,\n   379\t        nb_bytes_expected: message_size,\n   380\t        nb_bytes_received: 0,\n   381\t        nb_bytes_sent: 0,\n   382\t    };\n   383\t    connection.mark_active_stream(stream_id, true, Some(Box::new(stream_ctx)))\n   384\t}\n   385\t\n   386\t/// Create a new client QUIC connection and start it.\n   387\t/// C: `cnx_stress_create_client_cnx`.\n   388\tfn cnx_stress_create_client_cnx(ctx: &mut CnxStressCtx) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   389\t    let simulated_time = ctx.simulated_time();\n   390\t    let server_addr = ctx.server_addr;\n   391\t    let rank = {\n   392\t        let shared = ctx.shared.borrow();\n   393\t        shared.nb_clients\n   394\t    };\n   395\t\n   396\t    // Allocate a slot for the ConnectionId.\n   397\t    if rank >= ctx.client_connections.len() {\n   398\t        return Err(Error::Generic);\n   399\t    }\n   400\t\n   401\t    // Create the connection; set the callback before starting.\n   402\t    let cb = Box::new(CnxStressCallback {\n   403\t        shared: Rc::clone(&ctx.shared),\n   404\t        mode: 0,\n   405\t        rank,\n   406\t        streams: Vec::new(),\n   407\t    });\n   408\t    {\n   409\t        let shared = ctx.shared.borrow_mut();\n   410\t        let _ = shared; // just to keep borrow alive during build\n   411\t    }\n   412\t    let cnx_id_null = ConnectionId::with_size(0).ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n   413\t    let cnx = ctx\n   414\t        .qclient\n   415\t        .create_connection(\n   416\t            cnx_id_null,\n   417\t            cnx_id_null,\n   418\t            Some(&server_addr),\n   419\t            Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time),\n   420\t            0,\n   421\t            Some(crate::tests::util::TEST_SNI),\n   422\t            Some(CNX_STRESS_ALPN),\n   423\t            true,\n   424\t        )\n   425\t        .ok_or(Error::Memory)?;\n   426\t\n   427\t    // Store the connection's initial CID for later lookup.\n   428\t    let initial_cid = ConnectionId::with_size(0).ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n   429\t    cnx.set_callback(Some(cb));\n   430\t    cnx.enable_keep_alive(Duration::from_ticks(0));\n   431\t    cnx.start_client()?;\n   432\t\n   433\t    ctx.client_connections[rank] = Some(initial_cid);\n   434\t    ctx.shared.borrow_mut().c_active[rank] = true;\n   435\t    ctx.shared.borrow_mut().nb_clients += 1;\n   436\t    Ok(())\n   437\t}\n   438\t\n   439\t/// Close the next-in-line client connection.\n   440\t/// C: `cnx_stress_close_one_connection`.\n   441\tfn cnx_stress_close_one_connection(ctx: &mut CnxStressCtx) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   442\t    ctx.shared.borrow_mut().nb_clients_deleted += 1;\n   443\t    let rank = {\n   444\t        let shared = ctx.shared.borrow();\n   445\t        shared.nb_clients.saturating_sub(shared.nb_clients_deleted)\n   446\t    };\n   447\t    if let Some(Some(cid)) = ctx.client_connections.get(rank) {\n   448\t        let cid = *cid;\n   449\t        if let Some(cnx) = ctx.qclient.connection_ref_by_id(cid) {\n   450\t            cnx.close(0)?;\n   451\t        }\n   452\t    }\n   453\t    Ok(())\n   454\t}\n   455\t\n   456\t/// Dequeue one packet from `link` and deliver it to `quic`.\n   457\t/// C: `cnx_stress_link_arrival`.\n   458\tfn cnx_stress_link_arrival(\n   459\t    quic: &mut Quic,\n   460\t    link: &mut TestSimLink,\n   461\t    current_time: Instant,\n   462\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   463\t    if let Some(mut packet) = link.dequeue(current_time) {\n   464\t        quic.incoming_packet(\n   465\t            &mut packet.bytes[..packet.length],\n   466\t            &packet\n   467\t                .addr_from\n   468\t                .unwrap_or(SocketAddr::from(([0u8; 4], 0u16))),\n   469\t            &packet.addr_to.unwrap_or(SocketAddr::from(([0u8; 4], 0u16))),\n   470\t            0,\n   471\t            0,\n   472\t            current_time,\n   473\t        )?;\n   474\t    }\n   475\t    Ok(())\n   476\t}\n   477\t\n   478\t/// Prepare and send one outbound packet from `quic` onto `link`.\n   479\t/// C: `cnx_stress_prepare`.\n   480\tfn cnx_stress_prepare(\n   481\t    quic: &mut Quic,\n   482\t    link: &mut TestSimLink,\n   483\t    default_source: SocketAddr,\n   484\t    current_time: Instant,\n   485\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   486\t    let mut packet = TestSimPacket::create()?;\n   487\t    let prepared = quic.prepare_next_packet(current_time, &mut packet.bytes)?;\n   488\t    if prepared.send_length > 0 {\n   489\t        packet.length = prepared.send_length;\n   490\t        packet.addr_to = Some(prepared.addr_to);\n   491\t        let addr_from = if prepared.addr_from.ip().is_unspecified() {\n   492\t            default_source\n   493\t        } else {\n   494\t            prepared.addr_from\n   495\t        };\n   496\t        packet.addr_from = Some(addr_from);\n   497\t        link.submit(packet, current_time);\n   498\t    }\n   499\t    Ok(())\n   500\t}\n   501\t\n   502\t/// Events the simulation loop can dispatch.\n   503\t/// C: `cnx_stress_event_enum`.\n   504\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n   505\tenum CnxStressEvent {\n   506\t    None,\n   507\t    NewMessage,\n   508\t    ClientCreation,\n   509\t    ClientRemoval,\n   510\t    ClientArrival,\n   511\t    ClientPrepare,\n   512\t    ServerArrival,\n   513\t    ServerPrepare,\n   514\t}\n   515\t\n   516\t/// Run one step of the simulation, advancing `simulated_time` to the next\n   517\t/// scheduled event and executing it.  C: `cnx_stress_loop_step`.\n   518\tfn cnx_stress_loop_step(ctx: &mut CnxStressCtx) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   519\t    let simulated_time = ctx.simulated_time();\n   520\t\n   521\t    let mut next_event = CnxStressEvent::None;\n   522\t    let mut next_time = u64::MAX;\n   523\t\n   524\t    macro_rules! maybe_event {\n   525\t        ($event:expr, $time:expr) => {\n   526\t            if $time < next_time {\n   527\t                next_event = $event;\n   528\t                next_time = $time;\n   529\t            }\n   530\t        };\n   531\t    }\n   532\t\n   533\t    maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::NewMessage, ctx.next_message_creation_time);\n   534\t    maybe_event!(\n   535\t        CnxStressEvent::ClientCreation,\n   536\t        ctx.next_client_creation_time\n   537\t    );\n   538\t    maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::ClientRemoval, ctx.next_client_deletion_time);\n   539\t\n   540\t    // Next packet arrival on the link to clients.\n   541\t    if let Some(first) = ctx.link_to_clients.packets.front() {\n   542\t        maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::ClientArrival, first.arrival_time.ticks());\n   543\t    }\n   544\t    // Next time the client QUIC context wants to act.\n   545\t    let client_wake = ctx\n   546\t        .qclient\n   547\t        .next_wake_time(Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time));\n   548\t    maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::ClientPrepare, client_wake);\n   549\t\n   550\t    // Next packet arrival on the link to server.\n   551\t    if let Some(first) = ctx.link_to_server.packets.front() {\n   552\t        maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::ServerArrival, first.arrival_time.ticks());\n   553\t    }\n   554\t    // Next time the server QUIC context wants to act.\n   555\t    let server_wake = ctx\n   556\t        .qserver\n   557\t        .next_wake_time(Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time));\n   558\t    maybe_event!(CnxStressEvent::ServerPrepare, server_wake);\n   559\t\n   560\t    // Advance simulated time.\n   561\t    if next_time > simulated_time {\n   562\t        ctx.shared.borrow_mut().simulated_time = next_time;\n   563\t    }\n   564\t    let now = Instant::from_ticks(ctx.simulated_time());\n   565\t\n   566\t    match next_event {\n   567\t        CnxStressEvent::NewMessage => {\n   568\t            cnx_stress_initiate_message(ctx)?;\n   569\t            let target = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_messages_target;\n   570\t            let sent = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_messages_sent;\n   571\t            if sent >= target {\n   572\t                ctx.next_message_creation_time = u64::MAX;\n   573\t            } else {\n   574\t                ctx.next_message_creation_time += ctx.message_creation_interval;\n   575\t            }\n   576\t        }\n   577\t        CnxStressEvent::ClientCreation => {\n   578\t            cnx_stress_create_client_cnx(ctx)?;\n   579\t            let nb = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_clients;\n   580\t            let target = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_client_target;\n   581\t            if nb >= target {\n   582\t                ctx.next_client_creation_time = u64::MAX;\n   583\t            } else {\n   584\t                ctx.next_client_creation_time += ctx.client_creation_interval;\n   585\t            }\n   586\t        }\n   587\t        CnxStressEvent::ClientRemoval => {\n   588\t            cnx_stress_close_one_connection(ctx)?;\n   589\t            let deleted = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_clients_deleted;\n   590\t            let nb = ctx.shared.borrow().nb_clients;\n   591\t            if deleted >= nb {\n   592\t                ctx.next_client_deletion_time = u64::MAX;\n   593\t            } else {\n   594\t                ctx.next_client_deletion_time += ctx.client_deletion_interval;\n   595\t            }\n   596\t        }\n   597\t        CnxStressEvent::ClientArrival => {\n   598\t            cnx_stress_link_arrival(&mut ctx.qclient, &mut ctx.link_to_clients, now)?;\n   599\t        }\n   600\t        CnxStressEvent::ClientPrepare => {\n   601\t            cnx_stress_prepare(\n   602\t                &mut ctx.qclient,\n   603\t                &mut ctx.link_to_server,\n   604\t                ctx.client_addr,\n   605\t                now,\n   606\t            )?;\n   607\t        }\n   608\t        CnxStressEvent::ServerArrival => {\n   609\t            cnx_stress_link_arrival(&mut ctx.qserver, &mut ctx.link_to_server, now)?;\n   610\t        }\n   611\t        CnxStressEvent::ServerPrepare => {\n   612\t            cnx_stress_prepare(\n   613\t                &mut ctx.qserver,\n   614\t                &mut ctx.link_to_clients,\n   615\t                ctx.server_addr,\n   616\t                now,\n   617\t            )?;\n   618\t        }\n   619\t        CnxStressEvent::None => return Err(Error::Generic),\n   620\t    }\n   621\t\n   622\t    Ok(())\n   623\t}\n   624\t\n   625\t/// Set transport parameters suitable for the stress test.\n   626\t/// C: `cnx_stress_set_default_tp`.\n   627\tfn cnx_stress_set_default_tp(quic: &mut Quic) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   628\t    let tp = TransportParameters {\n   629\t        initial_max_stream_data_bidi_local: 0,\n   630\t        initial_max_stream_data_bidi_remote: 0,\n   631\t        initial_max_stream_id_bidir: 0,\n   632\t        initial_max_stream_data_uni: 0x20000,\n   633\t        initial_max_stream_id_unidir: 64,\n   634\t        initial_max_data: 0x20000,\n   635\t        max_idle_timeout: Duration::from_ticks(60_000_000), // 60 s in µs\n   636\t        max_packet_size: crate::MAX_PACKET_SIZE as u32,\n   637\t        max_ack_delay: 10_000,\n   638\t        active_connection_id_limit: 3,\n   639\t        ack_delay_exponent: 3,\n   640\t        migration_disabled: false,\n   641\t        ..Default::default()\n   642\t    };\n   643\t    quic.set_default_tp(&tp)\n   644\t}\n   645\t\n   646\t/// Build the full stress-test context.\n   647\t/// C: `cnx_stress_create_ctx`.\n   648\tfn cnx_stress_create_ctx(\n   649\t    duration: u64,\n   650\t    nb_clients: usize,\n   651\t    limit_test: bool,\n   652\t) -> Option<CnxStressCtx> {\n   653\t    let limit_extra = limit_test as usize;\n   654\t    let nb_slots = nb_clients + limit_extra;\n   655\t\n   656\t    // Validate timing parameters.\n   657\t    let client_creation_interval = 2_000u64;\n   658\t    let client_deletion_interval = 100u64;\n   659\t    if (client_creation_interval + client_deletion_interval) * nb_clients as u64 > duration {\n   660\t        return None;\n   661\t    }\n   662\t    let next_client_deletion_time = duration - client_deletion_interval * nb_clients as u64;\n   663\t    let nb_messages_target = nb_clients.min(20_000);\n   664\t    let message_size = 1024u64;\n   665\t    let message_creation_interval = next_client_deletion_time\n   666\t        .checked_div(3 * nb_messages_target as u64)\n   667\t        .filter(|&x| x > 0)?;\n   668\t    let next_message_creation_time = next_client_deletion_time / 3;\n   669\t\n   670\t    // Seed the deterministic RNG the same way as C.  C: `picoquic_test_random`.\n   671\t    let mut random_ctx = 0xBABAC001BADDBAB1_u64 ^ duration ^ (nb_clients as u64);\n   672\t    test_random(&mut random_ctx);\n   673\t    test_random(&mut random_ctx);\n   674\t\n   675\t    // Shared mutable state.\n   676\t    let shared = Rc::new(RefCell::new(CnxStressShared {\n   677\t        nb_clients: 0,\n   678\t        nb_servers: 0,\n   679\t        nb_clients_deleted: 0,\n   680\t        c_active: vec![false; nb_slots],\n   681\t        s_active: vec![false; nb_slots],\n   682\t        is_limit_test: limit_test,\n   683\t        limit_test_got_server_busy: false,\n   684\t        nb_client_target: nb_clients + limit_extra,\n   685\t        nb_messages_target,\n   686\t        message_size,\n   687\t        nb_messages_sent: 0,\n   688\t        nb_messages_errors: 0,\n   689\t        nb_messages_received: 0,\n   690\t        sum_message_delays: 0,\n   691\t        sum_square_message_delays: 0.0,\n   692\t        message_delay_min: i64::MAX,\n   693\t        message_delay_max: 0,\n   694\t        simulated_time: 0,\n   695\t    }));\n   696\t\n   697\t    let simulated_time = 0u64;\n   698\t\n   699\t    // Default server callback (mode == 2).\n   700\t    let default_cb = Box::new(CnxStressCallback {\n   701\t        shared: Rc::clone(&shared),\n   702\t        mode: 2,\n   703\t        rank: 0,\n   704\t        streams: Vec::new(),\n   705\t    });\n   706\t\n   707\t    let client_addr = SocketAddr::from(([8u8, 8, 8, 8], 12345u16));\n   708\t    let server_addr = SocketAddr::from(([1u8, 1, 1, 1], 4433u16));\n   709\t\n   710\t    let mut qclient = Quic::new(\n   711\t        nb_slots as u32,\n   712\t        None,\n   713\t        None,\n   714\t        None,\n   715\t        Some(CNX_STRESS_ALPN),\n   716\t        None,\n   717\t        None,\n   718\t        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n   719\t        Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time),\n   720\t        None,\n   721\t        None,\n   722\t    )?;\n   723\t\n   724\t    let mut qserver = Quic::new(\n   725\t        nb_clients as u32,\n   726\t        Some(TEST_FILE_SERVER_CERT),\n   727\t        Some(TEST_FILE_SERVER_KEY),\n   728\t        None,\n   729\t        Some(CNX_STRESS_ALPN),\n   730\t        Some(default_cb),\n   731\t        None,\n   732\t        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n   733\t        Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time),\n   734\t        None,\n   735\t        None,\n   736\t    )?;\n   737\t\n   738\t    let link_to_clients = Box::new(\n   739\t        TestSimLink::create(\n   740\t            1.0,\n   741\t            10_000,\n   742\t            None,\n   743\t            20_000,\n   744\t            Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time),\n   745\t        )\n   746\t        .ok()?,\n   747\t    );\n   748\t    let link_to_server = Box::new(\n   749\t        TestSimLink::create(\n   750\t            1.0,\n   751\t            10_000,\n   752\t            None,\n   753\t            20_000,\n   754\t            Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time),\n   755\t        )\n   756\t        .ok()?,\n   757\t    );\n   758\t\n   759\t    qclient.set_low_memory_mode(true).ok()?;\n   760\t    qserver.set_low_memory_mode(true).ok()?;\n   761\t    cnx_stress_set_default_tp(&mut qclient).ok()?;\n   762\t    cnx_stress_set_default_tp(&mut qserver).ok()?;\n   763\t\n   764\t    Some(CnxStressCtx {\n   765\t        shared,\n   766\t        qserver,\n   767\t        qclient,\n   768\t        server_addr,\n   769\t        client_addr,\n   770\t        link_to_clients,\n   771\t        link_to_server,\n   772\t        client_creation_interval,\n   773\t        next_client_creation_time: 0,\n   774\t        client_deletion_interval,\n   775\t        next_client_deletion_time,\n   776\t        message_creation_interval,\n   777\t        next_message_creation_time,\n   778\t        client_connections: vec![None; nb_slots],\n   779\t        server_connections: vec![None; nb_slots],\n   780\t    })\n   781\t}\n   782\t\n   783\t/// Run the full stress test for `duration` µs with `nb_clients` connections.\n   784\t/// C: `cnx_stress_do_test`.\n   785\tfn cnx_stress_do_test(duration: u64, nb_clients: usize, do_report: bool) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   786\t    let mut ctx = cnx_stress_create_ctx(duration, nb_clients, false).ok_or(Error::Generic)?;\n   787\t\n   788\t    let wall_time_start = current_time();\n   789\t\n   790\t    while ctx.simulated_time() < duration {\n   791\t        cnx_stress_loop_step(&mut ctx)?;\n   792\t    }\n   793\t\n   794\t    let wall_time_elapsed = current_time() - wall_time_start;\n   795\t    let simulated = ctx.simulated_time();\n   796\t    let shared = ctx.shared.borrow();\n   797\t\n   798\t    // If real time exceeded simulated time, the implementation is too slow.\n   799\t    assert!(\n   800\t        wall_time_elapsed <= simulated,\n   801\t        \"wall time {wall_time_elapsed} µs exceeded simulated time {simulated} µs\",\n   802\t    );\n   803\t    assert_eq!(\n   804\t        shared.nb_clients, shared.nb_client_target,\n   805\t        \"client count mismatch\",\n   806\t    );\n   807\t    assert_eq!(\n   808\t        shared.nb_servers, shared.nb_client_target,\n   809\t        \"server count mismatch\",\n   810\t    );\n   811\t    assert_eq!(\n   812\t        shared.nb_messages_received, shared.nb_messages_target,\n   813\t        \"messages received mismatch: sent {}, received {}\",\n   814\t        shared.nb_messages_sent, shared.nb_messages_received,\n   815\t    );\n   816\t\n   817\t    if do_report {\n   818\t        let msg_avg_delay = if shared.nb_messages_target > 0 {\n   819\t            shared.sum_message_delays as f64 / shared.nb_messages_target as f64 / 1_000_000.0\n   820\t        } else {\n   821\t            0.0\n   822\t        };\n   823\t        println!(\"Many connection stress (cnx_stress) succeeds:\");\n   824\t        println!(\n   825\t            \"Processed {} connections for {}s (simulated) in {}s (wall time).\",\n   826\t            shared.nb_client_target,\n   827\t            simulated as f64 / 1_000_000.0,\n   828\t            wall_time_elapsed as f64 / 1_000_000.0,\n   829\t        );\n   830\t        println!(\n   831\t            \"Processed {} messages, delays min/avg/max= {}s, {}s, {}s.\",\n   832\t            shared.nb_messages_target,\n   833\t            shared.message_delay_min as f64 / 1_000_000.0,\n   834\t            msg_avg_delay,\n   835\t            shared.message_delay_max as f64 / 1_000_000.0,\n   836\t        );\n   837\t    }\n   838\t\n   839\t    Ok(())\n   840\t}\n   841\t\n   842\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   843\t// Test entry points.\n   844\t\n   845\t/// C: `cnx_limit_test` in `picoquictest/cnxstress.c`.\n   846\t///\n   847\t/// Verifies that creating a connection when the server is at capacity causes\n   848\t/// the connection to be rejected with `SERVER_BUSY`.\n   849\t#[test]\n   850\tfn cnx_limit() {\n   851\t    let nb_clients = 4usize;\n   852\t    let duration = 120_000_000u64;\n   853\t\n   854\t    let mut ctx = cnx_stress_create_ctx(duration, nb_clients, true).expect(\"create stress context\");\n   855\t\n   856\t    // Run until all `nb_clients` connections are up on both sides and at least\n   857\t    // at `ClientAlmostReady`.\n   858\t    let mut is_done = false;\n   859\t    while !is_done && ctx.simulated_time() < duration {\n   860\t        cnx_stress_loop_step(&mut ctx).expect(\"loop step\");\n   861\t\n   862\t        let (nb_c, nb_s) = {\n   863\t            let shared = ctx.shared.borrow();\n   864\t            (shared.nb_clients, shared.nb_servers)\n   865\t        };\n   866\t        if nb_c == nb_clients && nb_s == nb_clients {\n   867\t            // Check that every client slot has a connection at AlmostReady or beyond.\n   868\t            is_done = true;\n   869\t            for c in 0..nb_clients {\n   870\t                let ok = if let Some(Some(cid)) = ctx.client_connections.get(c) {\n   871\t                    let cid = *cid;\n   872\t                    if let Some(cnx) = ctx.qclient.connection_ref_by_id(cid) {\n   873\t                        cnx.state() >= State::ClientAlmostReady\n   874\t                    } else {\n   875\t                        false\n   876\t                    }\n   877\t                } else {\n   878\t                    false\n   879\t                };\n   880\t                if !ok {\n   881\t                    is_done = false;\n   882\t                    break;\n   883\t                }\n   884\t            }\n   885\t        }\n   886\t    }\n   887\t    assert!(\n   888\t        is_done,\n   889\t        \"failed to reach ClientAlmostReady for all connections\"\n   890\t    );\n   891\t\n   892\t    // Now attempt one extra connection (beyond the server's limit).\n   893\t    {\n   894\t        let mut shared = ctx.shared.borrow_mut();\n   895\t        shared.is_limit_test = true;\n   896\t        shared.nb_client_target += 1;\n   897\t    }\n   898\t    ctx.next_client_creation_time = ctx.simulated_time();\n   899\t\n   900\t    while ctx.simulated_time() < duration {\n   901\t        cnx_stress_loop_step(&mut ctx).expect(\"limit loop step\");\n   902\t        if ctx.shared.borrow().limit_test_got_server_busy {\n   903\t            break;\n   904\t        }\n   905\t    }\n   906\t    assert!(\n   907\t        ctx.shared.borrow().limit_test_got_server_busy,\n   908\t        \"server did not send SERVER_BUSY when at connection limit\",\n   909\t    );\n   910\t}\n   911\t\n   912\t/// C: `cnx_stress_unit_test` in `picoquictest/cnxstress.c`.\n   913\t///\n   914\t/// Stress-tests 100 simultaneous QUIC connections over 120 seconds of\n   915\t/// simulated time, verifying that all connections establish and all messages\n   916\t/// are delivered.\n   917\t#[test]\n   918\tfn cnx_stress() {\n   919\t    cnx_stress_do_test(120_000_000, 100, false).expect(\"cnx_stress_do_test\");\n   920\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba rs/fq/src/tests/edge_cases.rs'","aggregated_output":"     1\t//! Test cases for `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n     2\t//!\n     3\t//! A collection of regression tests for edge cases typically discovered\n     4\t//! via the QUIC interop runner.  Many involve specific loss patterns during\n     5\t//! 0-RTT handshakes, idle-timeout negotiation, stream-reset interaction,\n     6\t//! initial-PTO behaviour, and crypto-handshake frame errors.\n     7\t\n     8\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n     9\t\n    10\tuse super::util::{\n    11\t    TestApiStreamDesc, TestTlsApiCtx, tls_api_close_with_losses, tls_api_connection_loop,\n    12\t    tls_api_data_sending_loop, tls_api_init_ctx, tls_api_init_ctx_ex,\n    13\t    tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify, tls_api_one_sim_round, tls_api_wait_for_timeout,\n    14\t};\n    15\tuse crate::internal::Version;\n    16\tuse crate::{ConnectionId, Instant, PacketContext};\n    17\t\n    18\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    19\t// Shared scenarios.  Passed to helpers once those are implemented.\n    20\t\n    21\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n    22\tstatic SCENARIO_EDGE_CASE: &[TestApiStreamDesc] = &[TestApiStreamDesc {\n    23\t    stream_id: 4,\n    24\t    previous_stream_id: 0,\n    25\t    q_len: 128,\n    26\t    r_len: 1_000,\n    27\t}];\n    28\t\n    29\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n    30\tstatic SCENARIO_EDGE_RESET: &[TestApiStreamDesc] = &[TestApiStreamDesc {\n    31\t    stream_id: 4,\n    32\t    previous_stream_id: 0,\n    33\t    q_len: 1_000_000,\n    34\t    r_len: 1_000_000,\n    35\t}];\n    36\t\n    37\t#[allow(dead_code)]\n    38\tstatic SCENARIO_RESET_AT: &[TestApiStreamDesc] = &[TestApiStreamDesc {\n    39\t    stream_id: 4,\n    40\t    previous_stream_id: 0,\n    41\t    q_len: 257,\n    42\t    r_len: 1_000_000,\n    43\t}];\n    44\t\n    45\t/// Set up a test context with the standard edge-case configuration: a\n    46\t/// CID of the form `{0xed, 0x9e, 0xca, 0x5e, edge_case_id, zero_rtt, 0, 0}`,\n    47\t/// optional 0-RTT first pass, and `nb_init_rounds` rounds of simulation\n    48\t/// with the given `loss_mask`.\n    49\t/// C: `edge_case_prepare` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n    50\tfn edge_case_prepare(\n    51\t    _edge_case_id: u8,\n    52\t    _zero_rtt: bool,\n    53\t    _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n    54\t    _loss_mask: u64,\n    55\t    _nb_init_rounds: i32,\n    56\t) -> crate::Result<Box<TestTlsApiCtx>> {\n    57\t    todo!(\"edge_case_prepare: 0-RTT setup and partial simulation not yet implemented\")\n    58\t}\n    59\t\n    60\t/// Finish an edge-case test: run the connection loop, enable\n    61\t/// `immediate_exit`, drive data sending, and verify completion within\n    62\t/// `duration_max` µs.\n    63\t/// C: `edge_case_complete` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n    64\tfn edge_case_complete(\n    65\t    test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n    66\t    simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n    67\t    duration_max: u64,\n    68\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n    69\t    let mut loss_mask = 0u64;\n    70\t    tls_api_connection_loop(test_ctx, &mut loss_mask, 0, simulated_time)?;\n    71\t    test_ctx.immediate_exit = true;\n    72\t    tls_api_data_sending_loop(test_ctx, &mut loss_mask, simulated_time, 0)?;\n    73\t    tls_api_one_scenario_body_verify(test_ctx, simulated_time, duration_max)\n    74\t}\n    75\t\n    76\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    77\t// Reset-repeat test.\n    78\t\n    79\t/// Variant of the reset-repeat test: which frame event to exercise.\n    80\t/// C: `reset_test_enum` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n    81\tenum ResetTestKind {\n    82\t    AckMaxStream = 0,\n    83\t    AckReset,\n    84\t    ExtraMaxStream,\n    85\t    ExtraReset,\n    86\t    ExtraStop,\n    87\t    NeedMaxStream,\n    88\t    NeedReset,\n    89\t    NeedStop,\n    90\t}\n    91\t\n    92\t/// Establish a connection, start a large stream transfer, reset the stream\n    93\t/// on both sides, wait for the stream context to be freed, then exercise\n    94\t/// the specified post-reset frame event.\n    95\t/// C: `reset_repeat_test_one` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n    96\tfn reset_repeat_test_one(_kind: ResetTestKind) -> crate::Result<()> {\n    97\t    todo!(\"reset_repeat_test_one: stream-reset ACK/extra/need logic not yet implemented\")\n    98\t}\n    99\t\n   100\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   101\t// Idle-timeout test helpers.\n   102\t\n   103\t/// Verify idle-timeout negotiation: `client_timeout` and `server_timeout`\n   104\t/// (in ms) must negotiate to `expected_timeout` (in µs); assert the\n   105\t/// connection remains alive at half-time and drops by full-time.\n   106\t/// C: `idle_timeout_test_one` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   107\tfn idle_timeout_test_one(\n   108\t    _test_id: u8,\n   109\t    _client_timeout: u64,\n   110\t    _server_timeout: u64,\n   111\t    _expected_timeout: u64,\n   112\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   113\t    todo!(\"idle_timeout_test_one: idle-timeout negotiation loop not yet implemented\")\n   114\t}\n   115\t\n   116\t/// Verify that a client connecting to a non-responding server disconnects\n   117\t/// after `expected_timeout` µs (derived from `client_timeout` ms or\n   118\t/// `handshake_timeout` µs).\n   119\t/// C: `idle_server_test_one` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   120\tfn idle_server_test_one(\n   121\t    _test_id: u8,\n   122\t    _client_timeout: u64,\n   123\t    _handshake_timeout: u64,\n   124\t    _expected_timeout: u64,\n   125\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   126\t    todo!(\"idle_server_test_one: server-silent loop not yet implemented\")\n   127\t}\n   128\t\n   129\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   130\t// Initial-PTO helpers.\n   131\t\n   132\t/// Prepare the client's initial packet and submit it to the server to\n   133\t/// establish a crypto context on both sides.\n   134\t/// C: `initial_pto_prepare` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   135\tfn initial_pto_prepare(\n   136\t    _test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n   137\t    _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n   138\t) -> crate::Result<usize> {\n   139\t    todo!(\"initial_pto_prepare: prepare_packet + incoming_packet not yet implemented\")\n   140\t}\n   141\t\n   142\t/// Advance time until the client's next scheduled send, returning the packet\n   143\t/// length.  Stops early if the client enters a failure state.\n   144\t/// C: `initial_pto_wait` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   145\tfn initial_pto_wait(\n   146\t    _test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n   147\t    _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n   148\t    _max_wait: u64,\n   149\t) -> crate::Result<usize> {\n   150\t    todo!(\"initial_pto_wait: client next_wake_time loop not yet implemented\")\n   151\t}\n   152\t\n   153\t/// Craft a synthetic server ACK (Initial epoch) and deliver it to the client.\n   154\t/// C: `initial_pto_ack` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   155\tfn initial_pto_ack(\n   156\t    _test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n   157\t    _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n   158\t) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   159\t    todo!(\"initial_pto_ack: predict_header + format_ack + protect_packet not yet implemented\")\n   160\t}\n   161\t\n   162\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   163\t// Crypto-HS-offset helper.\n   164\t\n   165\t/// Inject a crypto handshake frame with a 64 KB offset into packet context\n   166\t/// `pc`, attempt the connection, and verify the client receives\n   167\t/// CRYPTO_BUFFER_EXCEEDED or IDLE_TIMEOUT.\n   168\t/// C: `crypto_hs_offset_test_one` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   169\tfn crypto_hs_offset_one(_pc: PacketContext) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   170\t    todo!(\"crypto_hs_offset_one: queue_misc_frame + connection loop not yet implemented\")\n   171\t}\n   172\t\n   173\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   174\t// Reset-stream-at helper.\n   175\t\n   176\t/// Variant for `reset_stream_at_test_one`.\n   177\t/// C: `reset_stream_at_test_enum` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   178\tenum ResetStreamAtSpec {\n   179\t    /// Reset just past what was already received.\n   180\t    Basic,\n   181\t    /// Reset exactly at the sent offset.\n   182\t    Limit,\n   183\t    /// Reset past what was received with a lossy link.\n   184\t    Loss,\n   185\t}\n   186\t\n   187\t/// Establish a connection, start sending a 1 MB stream, wait a short\n   188\t/// time, then call `reset_stream_at` with the appropriate `reliable_size`.\n   189\t/// Verify that the scenario completes and that `reliable_size` bytes were\n   190\t/// delivered.\n   191\t/// C: `reset_stream_at_test_one` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   192\tfn reset_stream_at_test_one(_spec: ResetStreamAtSpec) -> crate::Result<()> {\n   193\t    todo!(\"reset_stream_at_test_one: reset_stream_at + data loop not yet implemented\")\n   194\t}\n   195\t\n   196\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   197\t// ec9a helper (unique body, not a shared helper in C).\n   198\t\n   199\t/// Run the server-only prepare loop for `ec9a_preemptive_amok`:\n   200\t/// advance simulated time through server wakes, counting sent packets,\n   201\t/// until the server's connection count drops to zero.  Returns\n   202\t/// `(send_count, repeat_duration_µs)`.\n   203\tfn ec9a_server_loop(\n   204\t    _test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n   205\t    _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n   206\t) -> crate::Result<(i32, u64)> {\n   207\t    todo!(\"ec9a_server_loop: prepare_next_packet_ex server loop not yet implemented\")\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t/// Check whether the server's stream `stream_id` has `reset_sent` set.\n   211\t/// C: `picoquic_find_stream(cnx_server, id)->reset_sent`.\n   212\tfn check_stream_reset_sent(_test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx, _stream_id: u64) -> bool {\n   213\t    todo!(\n   214\t        \"check_stream_reset_sent: arena deref of StreamToken to StreamHead::reset_sent not yet implemented\"\n   215\t    )\n   216\t}\n   217\t\n   218\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   219\t// Test entries.\n   220\t\n   221\t/// C: `crypto_hs_offset_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   222\t#[test]\n   223\tfn crypto_hs_offset() {\n   224\t    for pc in [\n   225\t        PacketContext::Initial,\n   226\t        PacketContext::Handshake,\n   227\t        PacketContext::Application,\n   228\t    ] {\n   229\t        crypto_hs_offset_one(pc).expect(\"crypto_hs_offset_one\");\n   230\t    }\n   231\t}\n   232\t\n   233\t/// Edge case zero: verify the common 0-RTT infrastructure works.\n   234\t/// C: `ec00_zero_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   235\t#[test]\n   236\tfn ec00_zero() {\n   237\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   238\t    let mut test_ctx =\n   239\t        edge_case_prepare(0x00, true, &mut simulated_time, 0, 4).expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   240\t    edge_case_complete(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, 100_000).expect(\"edge_case_complete\");\n   241\t    assert!(\n   242\t        test_ctx.cnx_client().nb_zero_rtt_acked > 0,\n   243\t        \"expected at least one 0-RTT packet acked\"\n   244\t    );\n   245\t}\n   246\t\n   247\t/// Second-flight NACK: client should recover even when the handshake ACK\n   248\t/// and HandshakeDone are lost.\n   249\t/// C: `ec2f_second_flight_nack_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   250\t#[test]\n   251\tfn ec2f_second_flight() {\n   252\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   253\t    let initial_losses = 0x1c1u64;\n   254\t    let mut test_ctx = edge_case_prepare(0x2f, true, &mut simulated_time, initial_losses, 9)\n   255\t        .expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   256\t    // After 9 rounds: client must not yet be Ready; server must be Ready.\n   257\t    assert!(\n   258\t        !test_ctx.client_ready(),\n   259\t        \"client should not be ready yet after partial handshake\"\n   260\t    );\n   261\t    assert!(test_ctx.server_ready(), \"server should be ready\");\n   262\t    edge_case_complete(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, 360_000).expect(\"edge_case_complete\");\n   263\t}\n   264\t\n   265\t/// Fuzz 50 random loss patterns to look for corrupted retransmissions.\n   266\t/// C: `eccf_corrupted_file_fuzz_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   267\t#[test]\n   268\tfn eccf_corrupted_fuzz() {\n   269\t    // Runs 50 edge_case_prepare + edge_case_complete iterations with\n   270\t    // random loss masks derived from a deterministic seed.\n   271\t    todo!(\"eccf_corrupted_fuzz: random-loss fuzz loop not yet implemented\")\n   272\t}\n   273\t\n   274\t/// Amplification-limited handshake with a large server hello and losses.\n   275\t/// C: `eca1_amplification_loss_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   276\t#[test]\n   277\tfn eca1_amplification_loss() {\n   278\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   279\t    let mut test_ctx =\n   280\t        edge_case_prepare(0xa1, false, &mut simulated_time, 0x0FF4, 16).expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   281\t    edge_case_complete(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, 15_000_000).expect(\"edge_case_complete\");\n   282\t}\n   283\t\n   284\t/// Loss of the final closing packet: connection must close within 10 s.\n   285\t/// C: `ecf1_final_loss_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   286\t#[test]\n   287\tfn ecf1_final_loss() {\n   288\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   289\t    let mut test_ctx =\n   290\t        edge_case_prepare(0xf1, false, &mut simulated_time, 0, 20).expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   291\t    let mut zero_loss = 0u64;\n   292\t    tls_api_connection_loop(&mut test_ctx, &mut zero_loss, 0, &mut simulated_time)\n   293\t        .expect(\"connection loop\");\n   294\t    test_ctx.immediate_exit = true;\n   295\t    tls_api_data_sending_loop(&mut test_ctx, &mut zero_loss, &mut simulated_time, 0)\n   296\t        .expect(\"data sending loop\");\n   297\t    tls_api_close_with_losses(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, 0xb10)\n   298\t        .expect(\"close with losses\");\n   299\t    assert!(\n   300\t        simulated_time.ticks() <= 10_000_000,\n   301\t        \"connection close took too long: {} µs\",\n   302\t        simulated_time.ticks()\n   303\t    );\n   304\t}\n   305\t\n   306\t/// Silly CID: server sends a new CID frame that is dropped and later\n   307\t/// repeated in a bogus way.  Both sides must reach Ready.\n   308\t/// C: `ec5c_silly_cid_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   309\t#[test]\n   310\tfn ec5c_silly_cid() {\n   311\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   312\t    let mut test_ctx = edge_case_prepare(0x5c, false, &mut simulated_time, 0x01e084, 48)\n   313\t        .expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   314\t    assert!(test_ctx.has_cnx_server(), \"server connection must exist\");\n   315\t    assert!(test_ctx.client_ready(), \"client must be ready\");\n   316\t    assert!(test_ctx.server_ready(), \"server must be ready\");\n   317\t    edge_case_complete(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, 3_000_000).expect(\"edge_case_complete\");\n   318\t}\n   319\t\n   320\t/// After the client closes, the server must not send more than ~50 preemptive\n   321\t/// repeats and must stop within its idle timeout.\n   322\t/// C: `ec9a_preemptive_amok_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   323\t#[test]\n   324\tfn ec9a_preemptive_amok() {\n   325\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   326\t    let mut test_ctx =\n   327\t        edge_case_prepare(0x9a, false, &mut simulated_time, 0x800, 12).expect(\"edge_case_prepare\");\n   328\t    assert!(test_ctx.has_cnx_server(), \"server connection must exist\");\n   329\t    assert!(test_ctx.server_ready(), \"server must be in ready state\");\n   330\t    assert!(test_ctx.test_finished, \"data transfer must have completed\");\n   331\t    let (send_count, repeat_duration) =\n   332\t        ec9a_server_loop(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time).expect(\"server loop\");\n   333\t    assert!(\n   334\t        send_count <= 50,\n   335\t        \"server sent too many repeat packets: {send_count}\"\n   336\t    );\n   337\t    // repeat_duration must be <= idle_timeout (checked inside ec9a_server_loop)\n   338\t    let _ = repeat_duration;\n   339\t}\n   340\t\n   341\t/// C: `idle_timeout_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   342\t#[test]\n   343\tfn idle_timeout() {\n   344\t    idle_timeout_test_one(1, 30_000, 30_000, 30_000_000).expect(\"case 1\");\n   345\t    idle_timeout_test_one(2, 60_000, 20_000, 20_000_000).expect(\"case 2\");\n   346\t    idle_timeout_test_one(3, 20_000, 60_000, 20_000_000).expect(\"case 3\");\n   347\t    idle_timeout_test_one(4, 5_000, 300_000, 5_000_000).expect(\"case 4\");\n   348\t    idle_timeout_test_one(5, 300_000, 5_000, 5_000_000).expect(\"case 5\");\n   349\t    idle_timeout_test_one(6, 0, 5_000, 5_000_000).expect(\"case 6\");\n   350\t    idle_timeout_test_one(7, 0, 60_000, 60_000_000).expect(\"case 7\");\n   351\t    idle_timeout_test_one(8, 5_000, 0, 5_000_000).expect(\"case 8\");\n   352\t    idle_timeout_test_one(9, 60_000, 0, 60_000_000).expect(\"case 9\");\n   353\t    idle_timeout_test_one(10, 0, 0, u64::MAX).expect(\"case 10\");\n   354\t}\n   355\t\n   356\t/// C: `idle_server_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   357\t#[test]\n   358\tfn idle_server() {\n   359\t    idle_server_test_one(1, 30_000, 0, 30_100_000).expect(\"case 1\");\n   360\t    idle_server_test_one(2, 60_000, 0, 60_100_000).expect(\"case 2\");\n   361\t    idle_server_test_one(3, 5_000, 0, 5_100_000).expect(\"case 3\");\n   362\t    idle_server_test_one(4, 0, 0, 30_100_000).expect(\"case 4\");\n   363\t    idle_server_test_one(5, 0, 10_000, 10_100_000).expect(\"case 5\");\n   364\t    idle_server_test_one(6, 20_000, 60_000, 60_100_000).expect(\"case 6\");\n   365\t    idle_server_test_one(7, 60_000, 5_000, 5_100_000).expect(\"case 7\");\n   366\t}\n   367\t\n   368\t/// C: `initial_pto_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   369\t#[test]\n   370\tfn initial_pto() {\n   371\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   372\t    let initial_cid =\n   373\t        ConnectionId::clone_from_slice(&[0x94, 0x01, 0x41, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]).expect(\"8-byte CID\");\n   374\t    let simulated_rtt = 20_000u64;\n   375\t    let simulated_pto = 4 * simulated_rtt;\n   376\t\n   377\t    let mut test_ctx = tls_api_init_ctx_ex(\n   378\t        &mut simulated_time,\n   379\t        Version::InternalTest1 as u32,\n   380\t        None,\n   381\t        Some(&initial_cid),\n   382\t    )\n   383\t    .expect(\"tls_api_init_ctx_ex\");\n   384\t\n   385\t    test_ctx.qclient.set_qlog(\".\").ok();\n   386\t    test_ctx.cnx_client().start_client().expect(\"start_client\");\n   387\t\n   388\t    // Send the initial packet to the server.\n   389\t    let length =\n   390\t        initial_pto_prepare(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time).expect(\"initial_pto_prepare\");\n   391\t    assert!(length >= 1200, \"initial packet too short: {length}\");\n   392\t\n   393\t    // Wait until the ACK time, then send a synthetic ACK to the client.\n   394\t    if simulated_time.ticks() < simulated_rtt {\n   395\t        let _length = initial_pto_wait(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, simulated_rtt)\n   396\t            .expect(\"initial_pto_wait\");\n   397\t    }\n   398\t    initial_pto_ack(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time).expect(\"initial_pto_ack\");\n   399\t\n   400\t    // The client should fire a PTO and send at least 1200 bytes.\n   401\t    if simulated_time.ticks() < simulated_pto {\n   402\t        let length = initial_pto_wait(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, simulated_pto)\n   403\t            .expect(\"initial_pto_wait (PTO)\");\n   404\t        assert!(length >= 1200, \"PTO packet not sent (length = {length})\");\n   405\t    }\n   406\t}\n   407\t\n   408\t/// C: `initial_pto_srv_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   409\t#[test]\n   410\tfn initial_pto_srv() {\n   411\t    // Verify that the server's PTO includes both an Initial and a Handshake\n   412\t    // packet when the initial packet is not yet acknowledged.\n   413\t    todo!(\"initial_pto_srv: pto_server_prepare loop not yet implemented\")\n   414\t}\n   415\t\n   416\t/// C: `reset_ack_max_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   417\t#[test]\n   418\tfn reset_ack_max() {\n   419\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::AckMaxStream).expect(\"reset_ack_max\");\n   420\t}\n   421\t\n   422\t/// C: `reset_ack_reset_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   423\t#[test]\n   424\tfn reset_ack_reset() {\n   425\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::AckReset).expect(\"reset_ack_reset\");\n   426\t}\n   427\t\n   428\t/// C: `reset_extra_max_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   429\t#[test]\n   430\tfn reset_extra_max() {\n   431\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::ExtraMaxStream).expect(\"reset_extra_max\");\n   432\t}\n   433\t\n   434\t/// C: `reset_extra_reset_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   435\t#[test]\n   436\tfn reset_extra_reset() {\n   437\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::ExtraReset).expect(\"reset_extra_reset\");\n   438\t}\n   439\t\n   440\t/// C: `reset_extra_stop_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   441\t#[test]\n   442\tfn reset_extra_stop() {\n   443\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::ExtraStop).expect(\"reset_extra_stop\");\n   444\t}\n   445\t\n   446\t/// C: `reset_need_max_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   447\t#[test]\n   448\tfn reset_need_max() {\n   449\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::NeedMaxStream).expect(\"reset_need_max\");\n   450\t}\n   451\t\n   452\t/// C: `reset_need_reset_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   453\t#[test]\n   454\tfn reset_need_reset() {\n   455\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::NeedReset).expect(\"reset_need_reset\");\n   456\t}\n   457\t\n   458\t/// C: `reset_need_stop_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   459\t#[test]\n   460\tfn reset_need_stop() {\n   461\t    reset_repeat_test_one(ResetTestKind::NeedStop).expect(\"reset_need_stop\");\n   462\t}\n   463\t\n   464\t/// Reset a stream on the server side while it is still mid-transfer, then\n   465\t/// verify that the client correctly forbids adding data or marking it active\n   466\t/// after the reset.\n   467\t/// C: `reset_loop_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   468\t#[test]\n   469\tfn reset_loop_test() {\n   470\t    let mut simulated_time = Instant::from_ticks(0);\n   471\t    let test_stream: u64 = 8;\n   472\t\n   473\t    let mut test_ctx = tls_api_init_ctx(\n   474\t        &mut simulated_time,\n   475\t        crate::internal::Version::InternalTest1 as u32,\n   476\t        None,\n   477\t    )\n   478\t    .expect(\"tls_api_init_ctx\");\n   479\t\n   480\t    // The real callback (reset_loop_callback_t) tracks data_sent/received/fin/reset per\n   481\t    // stream rank; that trait object is not yet implemented in Rust.\n   482\t    test_ctx.qserver.set_default_callback(None);\n   483\t    test_ctx.cnx_client().set_callback(None);\n   484\t\n   485\t    test_ctx.cnx_client().start_client().expect(\"start_client\");\n   486\t\n   487\t    // Queue initial data on streams 4 and 8; triggers server-side stream creation.\n   488\t    let bogus = [0u8; 4];\n   489\t    test_ctx\n   490\t        .cnx_client()\n   491\t        .add_to_stream(4, &bogus, false)\n   492\t        .expect(\"add_to_stream 4\");\n   493\t    test_ctx\n   494\t        .cnx_client()\n   495\t        .add_to_stream(8, &bogus, false)\n   496\t        .expect(\"add_to_stream 8\");\n   497\t\n   498\t    let mut loss_mask = 0u64;\n   499\t    tls_api_connection_loop(&mut test_ctx, &mut loss_mask, 0, &mut simulated_time)\n   500\t        .expect(\"connection loop\");\n   501\t\n   502\t    // Enable streaming on both client streams with equal priority.\n   503\t    test_ctx\n   504\t        .cnx_client()\n   505\t        .mark_active_stream(4, true, None)\n   506\t        .expect(\"mark active 4\");\n   507\t    test_ctx\n   508\t        .cnx_client()\n   509\t        .mark_active_stream(8, true, None)\n   510\t        .expect(\"mark active 8\");\n   511\t    test_ctx\n   512\t        .cnx_client()\n   513\t        .set_stream_priority(4, 8)\n   514\t        .expect(\"set client priority 4\");\n   515\t    test_ctx\n   516\t        .cnx_client()\n   517\t        .set_stream_priority(8, 8)\n   518\t        .expect(\"set client priority 8\");\n   519\t\n   520\t    // Allow stream data to begin flowing before the reset.\n   521\t    let timeout = simulated_time.ticks() + 100_000;\n   522\t    tls_api_wait_for_timeout(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, timeout).expect(\"100ms wait\");\n   523\t\n   524\t    // Server resets stream 8 while the transfer is in progress.\n   525\t    test_ctx\n   526\t        .cnx_server()\n   527\t        .reset_stream(test_stream, 0)\n   528\t        .expect(\"reset_stream\");\n   529\t\n   530\t    // Adjust priorities to expose the bug (different priorities post-reset).\n   531\t    test_ctx\n   532\t        .cnx_client()\n   533\t        .set_stream_priority(4, 9)\n   534\t        .expect(\"client priority 4\");\n   535\t    test_ctx\n   536\t        .cnx_client()\n   537\t        .set_stream_priority(8, 7)\n   538\t        .expect(\"client priority 8\");\n   539\t    test_ctx\n   540\t        .cnx_server()\n   541\t        .set_stream_priority(4, 9)\n   542\t        .expect(\"server priority 4\");\n   543\t    test_ctx\n   544\t        .cnx_server()\n   545\t        .set_stream_priority(8, 7)\n   546\t        .expect(\"server priority 8\");\n   547\t\n   548\t    // Poll until the server's RESET_STREAM frame has actually been sent.\n   549\t    let deadline = Instant::from_ticks(simulated_time.ticks() + 100_000);\n   550\t    for _ in 0..16 {\n   551\t        let mut was_active = false;\n   552\t        tls_api_one_sim_round(\n   553\t            &mut test_ctx,\n   554\t            &mut simulated_time,\n   555\t            deadline,\n   556\t            &mut was_active,\n   557\t        )\n   558\t        .expect(\"sim round\");\n   559\t        if check_stream_reset_sent(&mut test_ctx, test_stream) {\n   560\t            break;\n   561\t        }\n   562\t    }\n   563\t    assert!(\n   564\t        check_stream_reset_sent(&mut test_ctx, test_stream),\n   565\t        \"server did not send RESET_STREAM for stream {test_stream}\"\n   566\t    );\n   567\t\n   568\t    // After reset, adding data or marking the stream active must be rejected.\n   569\t    assert!(\n   570\t        test_ctx\n   571\t            .cnx_server()\n   572\t            .add_to_stream(test_stream, &[1, 2, 3, 4], true)\n   573\t            .is_err(),\n   574\t        \"add_to_stream after reset should be forbidden on stream {test_stream}\"\n   575\t    );\n   576\t    assert!(\n   577\t        test_ctx\n   578\t            .cnx_server()\n   579\t            .mark_active_stream(test_stream, true, None)\n   580\t            .is_err(),\n   581\t        \"mark_active_stream after reset should be forbidden on stream {test_stream}\"\n   582\t    );\n   583\t\n   584\t    // Final loop: verify the connection settles within 2 seconds.\n   585\t    let timeout2 = simulated_time.ticks() + 2_000_000;\n   586\t    tls_api_wait_for_timeout(&mut test_ctx, &mut simulated_time, timeout2).expect(\"2s wait\");\n   587\t}\n   588\t\n   589\t/// C: `reset_stream_at_basic_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   590\t#[test]\n   591\tfn reset_stream_at_basic() {\n   592\t    reset_stream_at_test_one(ResetStreamAtSpec::Basic).expect(\"reset_stream_at_basic\");\n   593\t}\n   594\t\n   595\t/// C: `reset_stream_at_limit_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   596\t#[test]\n   597\tfn reset_stream_at_limit_test() {\n   598\t    reset_stream_at_test_one(ResetStreamAtSpec::Limit).expect(\"reset_stream_at_limit\");\n   599\t}\n   600\t\n   601\t/// C: `reset_stream_at_loss_test` in `picoquictest/edge_cases.c`.\n   602\t#[test]\n   603\tfn reset_stream_at_loss() {\n   604\t    reset_stream_at_test_one(ResetStreamAtSpec::Loss).expect(\"reset_stream_at_loss\");\n   605\t}\n   606\t\n   607\t/// Table-driven check that every named [`crate::errors::InternalError`]\n   608\t/// and [`crate::errors::TransportError`] code resolves to its\n   609\t/// short textual name, plus the four \"default-branch\" buckets\n   610\t/// (`crypto error alert`, `unknown picoquic error`, `unknown`).\n   611\t#[test]\n   612\tfn error_name() {\n   613\t    use crate::errors::InternalError;\n   614\t\n   615\t    let cases: &[(u64, &str)] = &[\n   616\t        // Protocol (transport / TLS) errors.\n   617\t        (0x1, \"internal\"),\n   618\t        (0x2, \"server busy\"),\n   619\t        (0x3, \"flow control\"),\n   620\t        (0x4, \"stream limit\"),\n   621\t        (0x5, \"stream state\"),\n   622\t        (0x6, \"final offset\"),\n   623\t        (0x7, \"frame format\"),\n   624\t        (0x8, \"parameter\"),\n   625\t        (0x9, \"connection_id limit\"),\n   626\t        (0xA, \"protocol violation\"),\n   627\t        (0xB, \"invalid token\"),\n   628\t        (0xC, \"application\"),\n   629\t        (0xD, \"crypto buffer exceeded\"),\n   630\t        (0xE, \"key update\"),\n   631\t        (0xF, \"aead limit\"),\n   632\t        (0x178, \"wrong alpn\"),\n   633\t        (0x201, \"tls handshake failed\"),\n   634\t        (0x11, \"version negotiation\"),\n   635\t        (0x3e, \"application abandon\"),\n   636\t        (0x3e75, \"resource limit reached\"),\n   637\t        (0x3e76, \"unstable interface\"),\n   638\t        (0x3e77, \"no CID available\"),\n   639\t        // Picoquic-internal codes (0x400+ range).\n   640\t        (0x401, \"duplicate\"),\n   641\t        (0x403, \"payload_decrypt_error\"),\n   642\t        (0x404, \"unexpected packet\"),\n   643\t        (0x405, \"memory\"),\n   644\t        (0x407, \"connection ID check\"),\n   645\t        (0x408, \"\"),\n   646\t        (0x409, \"version negotation spoofed\"),\n   647\t        (0x40A, \"malformed transport extension\"),\n   648\t        (0x40B, \"extension buffer too small\"),\n   649\t        (0x40C, \"illegal transport extension\"),\n   650\t        (0x40D, \"cannot reset the crypto stream\"),\n   651\t        (0x40E, \"invalid stream id\"),\n   652\t        (0x40F, \"stream already closed\"),\n   653\t        (0x410, \"frame buffer too small\"),\n   654\t        (0x411, \"invalid frame\"),\n   655\t        (0x412, \"cannot control the crypto stream\"),\n   656\t        (0x413, \"retry\"),\n   657\t        (0x414, \"disconnected\"),\n   658\t        (0x415, \"error detected\"),\n   659\t        (0x417, \"invalid ticket\"),\n   660\t        (0x418, \"invalid file\"),\n   661\t        (0x419, \"send buffer too small\"),\n   662\t        (0x41A, \"unexpected state\"),\n   663\t        (0x41B, \"unexpected error\"),\n   664\t        (0x41C, \"server configuration without cert\"),\n   665\t        (0x41D, \"no such file\"),\n   666\t        (0x41E, \"stateless reset\"),\n   667\t        (0x41F, \"connection deleted\"),\n   668\t        (0x420, \"connection ID segment error\"),\n   669\t        (0x421, \"connection ID not available\"),\n   670\t        (0x422, \"migration disabled\"),\n   671\t        (0x423, \"cannot compute key\"),\n   672\t        (0x424, \"cannot set active stream\"),\n   673\t        (0x425, \"cannot change active context\"),\n   674\t        (0x426, \"invalid token\"),\n   675\t        (0x427, \"initial CID too short\"),\n   676\t        (0x428, \"key rotation not ready\"),\n   677\t        (0x429, \"aead not ready\"),\n   678\t        (0x42A, \"no ALPN provided\"),\n   679\t        (0x42B, \"no callback provided\"),\n   680\t        (0x42C, \"stream receive complete\"),\n   681\t        (0x42D, \"packet header parsing\"),\n   682\t        (0x42E, \"QUIC bit missing\"),\n   683\t        (0x42F, \"terminate packet loop (not an error)\"),\n   684\t        (0x430, \"simulate NAT (not an error)\"),\n   685\t        (0x431, \"simulate migration (not an error)\"),\n   686\t        (0x432, \"version not supported\"),\n   687\t        (0x433, \"idle timeout\"),\n   688\t        (0x434, \"repeat timeout\"),\n   689\t        (0x435, \"handshake timeout\"),\n   690\t        (0x436, \"socket\"),\n   691\t        (0x437, \"version negotiation\"),\n   692\t        (0x438, \"packet too long\"),\n   693\t        (0x439, \"wrong version\"),\n   694\t        (0x43A, \"port blocked\"),\n   695\t        (0x43B, \"datagram too long\"),\n   696\t        (0x43C, \"invalid path ID\"),\n   697\t        (0x43D, \"retry needed\"),\n   698\t        (0x43E, \"server busy\"),\n   699\t        (0x43F, \"duplicate path\"),\n   700\t        (0x440, \"blocked by lack of path ID\"),\n   701\t        (0x441, \"blocked by lack of CID\"),\n   702\t        (0x442, \"path address family\"),\n   703\t        (0x443, \"path not ready\"),\n   704\t        (0x444, \"path limit exceeded\"),\n   705\t        (0x445, \"redirected to proxy (not an error)\"),\n   706\t        (0x446, \"padding_packet\"),\n   707\t        // CRYPTO_ERROR alert range (default branch).\n   708\t        (0x101, \"crypto error alert\"),\n   709\t        (0x150, \"crypto error alert\"),\n   710\t        (0x1FF, \"crypto error alert\"),\n   711\t        // Unknown picoquic error range (default branch).\n   712\t        (0x450, \"unknown picoquic error\"),\n   713\t        (0x4FF, \"unknown picoquic error\"),\n   714\t        // Truly unknown.\n   715\t        (0x0, \"unknown\"),\n   716\t        (0x200, \"unknown\"),\n   717\t        (0x500, \"unknown\"),\n   718\t        (0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF, \"unknown\"),\n   719\t    ];\n   720\t\n   721\t    for &(code, expected) in cases {\n   722\t        let got = InternalError::name(code).unwrap_or(\"<none>\");\n   723\t        assert_eq!(\n   724\t            got, expected,\n   725\t            \"error_code=0x{code:x} got={got:?} expected={expected:?}\",\n   726\t        );\n   727\t    }\n   728\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
